package dev.wildcatter.item;

import dev.wildcatter.Tuning;
import dev.wildcatter.energy.Voltage;
import dev.wildcatter.fluid.Reactor;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import net.minecraft.network.chat.Component;
import net.minecraft.server.network.Filterable;
import net.minecraft.world.item.component.WrittenBookContent;

/**
 * The text of the Field Manual. One page per string; add a chapter here whenever the mod gains something to explain.
 * Numbers come from Tuning, so the book can't drift out of date when something is rebalanced.
 */
public final class Manual {
	private Manual() {
	}

	public static WrittenBookContent content() {
		List<Filterable<Component>> pages = new ArrayList<>();
		for (String page : pages()) {
			pages.add(Filterable.passThrough(Component.literal(page)));
		}
		return new WrittenBookContent(Filterable.passThrough("Wildcatter Field Manual"), "Wildcatter", 0, pages, true);
	}

	private static List<String> pages() {
		double volts = Voltage.LOW.nominal();
		return List.of(
				"WILDCATTER\nField Manual\n\nPower from steam, gas and oil, built the way the real grid is: volts, amps, breakers and all.\n\nRead the safety pages before you touch anything.",

				"1. STEAM\n\nPut a Boiler (a small vertical boiler, 2 m tall) on a lit campfire. Fill it with water buckets (" + Tuning.WATER_PER_BUCKET + " each). "
						+ "Put a Steam Turbine touching it.\n\nOne campfire makes " + Math.round(Tuning.BOILER_STEAM_PER_TICK * 20 * Tuning.JOULES_PER_STEAM / 1000)
						+ " kW. Four buckets last about "
						+ (Tuning.BOILER_WATER_CAPACITY * Tuning.STEAM_PER_WATER / Tuning.BOILER_STEAM_PER_TICK / 20 / 60) + " minutes.\n\nThe turbine only burns steam for the power you actually use.",

				"2. THE LOOP\n\nElectricity needs a loop. Power leaves on a HOT wire (red) and comes back on a NEUTRAL wire (black). "
						+ "Every machine has to be joined to both.\n\nOne wire is a dead end: nothing flows and the lamp stays dark.",

				"3. OHM'S LAW\n\nVolts = Amps x Ohms\nWatts = Volts x Amps\n\nA " + Math.round(Tuning.LAMP_WATTS) + " W lamp on " + Math.round(volts)
						+ " V draws " + String.format("%.2f", Tuning.LAMP_WATTS / volts) + " A. A " + Math.round(Tuning.HEATER_WATTS) + " W heater draws "
						+ String.format("%.1f", Tuning.HEATER_WATTS / volts) + " A.\n\nRight-click anything with the Power Meter to see its real volts and amps.",

				"4. ADDING LOADS\n\nMachines wired across the same two wires are in parallel. Their amps ADD UP.\n\nTwo heaters: "
						+ String.format("%.1f", 2 * Tuning.HEATER_WATTS / volts) + " A. Add enough machines and the current passes what the wire "
						+ "and the breaker can take.",

				"5. BREAKERS\n\nPut a Breaker in the HOT wire: wire in at the back, out at the front. It opens the circuit when the current is too high.\n\n"
						+ "Overload: a little over its rating heats it until it trips; the further over, the faster.\nShort: " + (int) Tuning.BREAKER_MAGNETIC_MULTIPLE
						+ "x its rating trips it at once.\n\nRight-click: off/on, and reset. Sneak and right-click: change its rating.\n\nA breaker only guards what comes AFTER it. Put it first, right at the generator.",

				"6. WIRE RATINGS\n\nEvery wire has a maximum current set by its SIZE: " + (int) dev.wildcatter.energy.ConductorSize.AWG_12.amps() + " A for the 12 AWG wire you start with. Past it the wire heats up, over a minute or two: at twice the rating it burns out in about "
						+ Math.round(dev.wildcatter.energy.WireHeat.secondsToBurn(2)) + " seconds, a dead short at once. A motor's start, six times its current for a moment, does not hurt wire sized for it.\n\nA breaker protects the WIRE. Never fit a breaker rated higher than the wire it guards.\n\n"
						+ "Wire also has resistance: on a long run the voltage drops.",

				"7. SHORT CIRCUITS\n\nIf the hot and neutral touch with no load between them, the current is limited only by the wire: hundreds of amps. "
						+ "That is a short circuit.\n\nBare wires of opposite colour touching each other make one. A breaker trips at once. Without one, the wire burns out.",

				"8. WOOL INSULATION\n\nWool-wrapped wire is safe to touch and cannot short to a neighbour. But the wool wears: about "
						+ (int) (Tuning.WOOL_LIFE_TICKS / 24000) + " days of use, faster under heavy current, and " + (int) Tuning.WOOL_WET_WEAR
						+ "x faster in rain or water.\n\nWhen it is worn out it is bare wire again: it shocks and it can short. Check it. Replace it.\n\nBetter insulation needs plastic.",

				"9. VOLTAGE LEVELS\n\n" + Voltage.LOW.label() + ": lamps and small machines.\n" + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ": bigger generators and local lines.\n" + Voltage.HIGH.label() + ": long hauls.\n\n"
						+ "Wires only join at the same voltage. A TRANSFORMER joins two levels. The smallest are the POLE TRANSFORMERS, one for a " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " line and one for " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + ": the line goes to the top, the low side (one hot, one neutral) to the back. Higher voltage means fewer amps for the same power, which is why long lines use it. "
						+ "Windings lose a little to heat.",

				"10. SHOCKS\n\nBare live wire shocks anything near it. " + Voltage.LOW.label() + ": you must touch it. " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ": " + (int) Tuning.BARE_REACH_MEDIUM + " blocks. " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + ": "
						+ (int) Tuning.BARE_REACH_HIGH + " blocks, so keep bare lines up on tall poles.\n\n" + Voltage.LOW.label() + ": " + hearts(Tuning.SHOCK_DAMAGE_LOW) + " heart. " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ": "
						+ hearts(Tuning.SHOCK_DAMAGE_MEDIUM) + " hearts. " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + ": " + hearts(Tuning.SHOCK_DAMAGE_HIGH) + ".\nDouble if you are wet.",

				"11. GROUNDING\n\nPut a Ground Rod in the earth against a machine, or run Ground Wire from the machine to a rod. A grounded machine is safe to touch.\n\n"
						+ "An ungrounded machine with power in it may bite when you touch it: " + Math.round(Tuning.TOUCH_SHOCK_CHANCE_LOW * 100) + "% at " + Voltage.LOW.label() + ", "
						+ Math.round(Tuning.TOUCH_SHOCK_CHANCE_MEDIUM * 100) + "% at " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ", always at " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + ".",

				"12. POWER METER\n\nRight-click a wire, machine or breaker to read its volts, amps and watts, how worn the wool is, and whether a machine is grounded. "
						+ "It also says why a machine has no power.\n\nThe meter is insulated: safe on live equipment.",

				"FIREBOX\n\nRight-click a Firebox to open it and add coal, charcoal or wood. A hopper can feed it from any side. Put it under a Boiler and it heats it like a campfire (" + Math.round(Tuning.BOILER_STEAM_PER_TICK * 20 * Tuning.JOULES_PER_STEAM / 1000) + " kW).\n\n"
						+ "It only burns while the boiler wants heat, so a full steam tank costs no fuel.",

				"STEAM PLANT\n\nA " + Math.round(Tuning.PLANT_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " plant built from parts at their real size: 6 x 7 m and 4 m high, every part on the ground. Facing north: BURNER, BOILER and SUPERHEATER in the back row; GENERATOR and TURBINE in the middle row, the turbine under the superheater; FEED PUMP and CONDENSER in the front row, the condenser beside the turbine. The generator's readout names the next part it needs and where.\n\n"
						+ "Feed the burner coal (a coal block is a cubic metre: one coal is " + Math.round(Tuning.COAL_JOULES / 1e9 * 10) / 10.0 + " GJ, about a quarter hour at full power) or pipe PIPELINE GAS to it (see GAS PLANT: raw separator gas will not do). Right-click the generator to light it: the drum takes about " + Math.round(Tuning.PLANT_HEATUP_SECONDS / 60) + " minutes to reach pressure.\n\n"
						+ "The FEED PUMP is a " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " motor, wired at the box on its side: the plant needs power to start (a genset will do). The generator's cables connect at its end away from the turbine. Pipe water to the condenser for makeup, and put a COOLING TOWER's basin on that pipe, or the plant makes only three quarters of its rating. Its output goes through a GENERATOR STEP-UP transformer (delta to wye, the line side 30 degrees ahead) to " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + ".",

				"FULL-SIZE EQUIPMENT\n\nBig equipment is its real size: one block is a metre. Hold one and a green box shows where it will go (red if something is in the way); it faces away from you. Break any part of it and the whole thing comes down as one item.\n\n"
						+ "GENERATOR STEP-UP: 3 m across, 2 m deep, 3 m to the bushing tops. The " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " cable goes into the box low on the back, in the middle; the " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " leaves from the top of the three brown bushings: a cable on top of them, or beside them at the front.",

				"WATER\n\nPUMP: a " + Voltage.LOW.label() + " motor (" + Math.round(Tuning.PUMP_WATTS) + " W, " + String.format("%.1f", Tuning.PUMP_WATTS / Voltage.LOW.nominal()) + " A). Put it touching water, wire a hot and a neutral to it, and run PIPES to your boilers. "
						+ "It fills every boiler on its pipes. Low voltage slows it: its delivery follows the square of the voltage.\n\n"
						+ "DRAIN: a pipe touching a Steam Turbine carries its used steam back as water to the boilers on the same pipes. " + Math.round(Tuning.CONDENSATE_RETURN * 100) + "% comes back, so a loop still needs the pump. With no pipe the water is lost.",

				"FINDING OIL\n\nOil and gas hide in pockets deep underground. Use the SEISMOGRAPH (right-click): it thumps the ground and tells you which way the nearest pocket lies, how far, and how deep its top is. "
						+ "It cannot tell oil from gas: only a drill finds that out.\n\nPockets are about " + (Tuning.FIELD_MIN_RADIUS * 2) + "-" + (Tuning.FIELD_MAX_RADIUS * 2) + " blocks across. Walk toward a stronger echo. "
						+ "DEEP fields lie just above the bedrock, bigger and richer: a DEEP ECHO means only a LAND RIG reaches it. The oil is not in the rock to mine: only a well brings it up.",

				"DRILLING\n\nThe DRILLING RIG is a small mast rig, real size: a 6 m skid with a 9 m mast. Click the ground where the hole goes and the rig lies back from it, away from you. Feed its power unit's terminal box (low on the back end) " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " three-phase: its drive is a " + Math.round(Tuning.RIG_WATTS / 1000) + " kW motor (about " + Math.round(Tuning.RIG_WATTS / (3 * Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.nominal() * Tuning.MOTOR_POWER_FACTOR)) + " A a phase; use a 60 A three-pole breaker and three-phase cable). It sinks a steel-cased hole, a block a second at full voltage. Low voltage drills slowly.\n\n"
						+ "It reaches " + Tuning.SMALL_RIG_MAX_DEPTH + " m: deeper, it stops TOO DEEP. The top head turns the drill pipe and slides down the mast, a 6 m joint at a time. The CASING it leaves is cemented in: nothing breaks it. Reach the pocket and it STRIKES: the rig RIGS DOWN, drops as its item, and leaves a WELLHEAD on the hole: an OIL WELLHEAD or a gas CHRISTMAS TREE. Miss, and you get a DRY HOLE: break the rig and try again.",

				"OIL AND GAS WELLS\n\nCHRISTMAS TREE (gas wellhead, 2 m of valves): gas comes up by its own pressure, no power needed. Put a Firebox against its bottom, or run STEEL PIPES (the dark pipes, crafted from STEEL INGOTS: smelt iron ingots in a blast furnace) to fireboxes or a SEPARATOR. It only opens as far as something takes its gas. The gas comes up WET, with condensate and water: a firebox burns it, but a gas engine needs it separated.\n\n"
						+ "PUMPJACK (oil): 7 m long and 5 m tall. Stand behind where it goes and click the OIL WELLHEAD with it: it sets its horsehead over the well. Its " + String.format("%.1f", Tuning.PUMPJACK_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " three-phase motor (wire its terminal box, low at the back end, on the back or a side) turns the crank at " + Math.round(Tuning.PUMPJACK_SPM) + " strokes a minute and runs only while its flowline has room. The well brings up oil, WATER and GAS together: " + Math.round(Tuning.WATER_CUT_NEW * 100) + "% water when new, rising to " + Math.round(Tuning.WATER_CUT_DEPLETED * 100) + "% as the pocket drains. Run steel pipe from the wellhead to a SEPARATOR (see THE LEASE), or straight to fireboxes, which burn it as it comes.\n\n"
						+ "Wells on the same pocket share it, and the PRESSURE drops as it empties: the flow slows. Read it with the Power Meter.",

				"LAND RIG\n\nThe big rig: 1,000 hp, fed " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " three-phase (MV CABLE) at the west end of its DRIVE HOUSE. Put the SUBSTRUCTURE (9 x 9 m, 6 m high) over the hole first; click the MAST and DRAWWORKS on its floor, and the MUD TANKS, two MUD PUMPS and DRIVE HOUSE on the ground near it: each goes to its place. Its readout names what is missing. Click the TOP DRIVE into the mast, pipe water from a pump to the mud tanks, and right-click the substructure (the driller's console) to drill.\n\n"
						+ "It wants " + Math.round(Tuning.LAND_RIG_DRILL_WATTS / 1e6 * 10) / 10.0 + " MW while drilling. Short of power, it holds the frequency up and drills slower. It drills 5 times as fast as the small rig, a 27 m stand at a time, to any depth: the only rig for DEEP fields. On a strike the wellhead goes in the cellar under its floor.",

				"WORLD RULES\n\nSome rules change what an existing plant does, so each world keeps its own. A new world starts with them on, except cascadeSpinUp, reactorContamination and realResidenceTimes; a world from before them has them all off. An operator lists them with /wildcatter rule and sets one with /wildcatter rule <name> true or false.\n\nTIME SCALE: 1:1, 5:1, 10:1, 20:1 or 50:1. It shortens the long waits only (a real reactor heat-up and cooldown, the residence holds, cask cooling, other mods' cures): at 10:1 an 18 h coking takes 1.8 h. Rates, fuel and electrics stay real. Chosen on the Create World screen (World Rules..., with the rules themselves); an older world is 1:1. /wildcatter rule timeScale <1|5|10|20|50> changes it.\n\n"
						+ "saltDomeGrid192 (salt domes on a grid, with oil on their flanks), mudGel (LOW GEL), wellControl (kicks, the BOP, washouts), fluorinatorAshBed, cascadeSpinUp, the reactor's six, and realResidenceTimes (coking 18 h, digestion 1 h, precipitation 36 h held for real).",

				"SALT DOMES\n\nIn plains, swamps and on beaches a column of ROCK SALT rises from the deep under a calcite CAPROCK with native sulfur, a low hill over it. Salt seals the sand beds bent up against its flank: oil gathers there, in FLANK FIELDS, arcs round the dome " + Tuning.FLANK_MIN_WIDTH + " to " + Tuning.FLANK_MAX_WIDTH + " blocks wide, their tops at y " + Tuning.FLANK_MIN_Y + " to " + Tuning.FLANK_MAX_Y + ", richer than ordinary fields. Some domes hold a small CAPROCK POOL under the crest: it flows at full rate for its first " + Math.round(Tuning.CAPROCK_FLUSH * 100) + " %, then falls fast.\n\n"
						+ "The SEISMOGRAPH over a dome reads SALT DOME and its crest. A hole down the middle finds caprock, then salt, and no oil under it. Drill beside it: a flank well near the salt goes down through its edge (a land rig there needs salt-saturated mud).",

				"DRILLING MUD\n\nWater weighs " + String.format("%.2f", Tuning.WATER_KG_PER_L * Tuning.PPG_PER_KG_L) + " ppg (lb/gal). The land rig's tanks keep the mud's weight, gel and salt (its readout).\n\nMUD PLANT: a BARITE MILL (" + Math.round(Tuning.BARITE_MILL_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ", box on its west) grinds BARITE to API 13A 4.1; a BENTONITE DRYER (" + Math.round(Tuning.BENTONITE_MILL_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, gas or LPG on the east of its bottom) dries BENTONITE. Mineral by a hopper on top; a BAGGING STATION against each fills 1 t BULK BAGS.\n\n"
						+ "At the rig, a MUD HOPPER (" + Math.round(Tuning.MUD_HOPPER_WATTS / 1000) + " kW) against the mud tanks' east side (facing south, its box away from them) mixes a bag a minute from a hopper on top: BENTONITE gels the mud (under 15 lb/bbl it is LOW GEL and drills at half rate); BARITE weights it; ROCK SALT saturates it. Rock salt drilled with fresh mud WASHES OUT: the rig stops until the mud is salt-saturated. Water topping up thins the mud.",

				"THE LEASE\n\nSEPARATOR (36 in x 10 ft, no power): pipe the wells to its FRONT end. Out of its BACK end: GAS off the top, OIL from the upper cells, WATER from the lower cells, each on its own pipe.\n\nONE PRODUCT A PIPE: each joined run of steel pipe carries one thing. Where two meet (oil and water, say) the run is BLOCKED and nothing flows: the Power Meter on a pipe says what it carries.\n\nSLURRY: a concentrator's slurries (mill discharge, fines, conditioned, concentrate, thickened concentrate, tails) are counted in kg and carry an ASSAY, the minerals in each kg. Two sources on one pipe blend by mass; the Power Meter on the pipe names the richest minerals.\n\n"
						+ "OIL to a STOCK TANK (400 bbl, " + Math.round(Tuning.STOCK_TANK_LITERS / 1000) + " m3, any side of its bottom) or a crude unit; buckets fill and pour at the tank. GAS to fireboxes, gas engines and the steam plant burner; a FLARE STACK on the gas line burns only what they leave. WATER to a WATER TANK, then an INJECTION PUMP (" + Math.round(Tuning.INJECTION_PUMP_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " three-phase, over 110 A: feed it 4/0 cable; suction at its back end, discharge on top) into a DISPOSAL WELLHEAD set on a dry hole's casing.\n\nWith nowhere for oil, gas or water to go, the separator SHUTS IN and the wells stop.",

				"GAS TURBINE\n\nA 16.5 MW industrial gas turbine making " + Voltage.GENERATOR.label() + ". Against the TURBINE package: its INLET HOUSE, its GENERATOR, and an EXHAUST STACK (or an HRSG). The GENERATOR BREAKER goes against the generator's back end; GENERATOR BUS DUCT from the breaker to a 25 MVA GSU steps it up to " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + ".\n\n"
						+ "Fuel: PIPELINE GAS, DIESEL or KEROSENE into its west side (about 1.2 m3/s or 1.3 L/s at full load). To start it needs " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " at its STARTER box (west side, near the front): right-click, it purges a minute, lights and runs up, then closes its breaker. A LOAD BANK tests it.",

				"COMBINED CYCLE\n\nPut an HRSG against the turbine instead of its stack: the exhaust raises steam. A 5 MW STEAM TURBINE against the HRSG, its GENERATOR (with its own breaker) and an AIR-COOLED CONDENSER against the steam turbine, a FEED PUMP against the HRSG (fans and pump " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ").\n\nAt full load the plant makes about 21.7 MW from 46.9 MW of fuel: 46%, where the turbine alone makes 35%. At part load it does worse, as real ones do.",

				"PEAKER\n\nA 45 MW aeroderivative gas turbine for fast starts. Against the AERO TURBINE package: its INLET HOUSE, its GENERATOR and its EXHAUST STACK, laid out as for the 16.5 MW unit. The 3,000 A GENERATOR BREAKER goes against the generator's back end; 3,000 A GENERATOR BUS DUCT (three 1,200 A ducts and a copper block) to a 60 MVA GSU steps it up to " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + ".\n\n"
						+ "Starter and fuel as on the 16.5 MW unit (about 2.9 m3/s of gas or 3.1 L/s of oil at full load), but not coke oven gas: its low-emission fuel nozzles are tuned to pipeline gas, and a gas whose heat per square root of its density (its Wobbe index) is more than 10 % off is refused. Coker gas is close enough; burn coke oven gas in the 16.5 MW unit or a gas engine. It purges 30 s and runs up in a minute; on line it may take load at a quarter of its rating a minute, full load about five minutes after the button. The 16.5 MW unit takes 10% a minute.\n\n"
						+ "SUBSTATION 60 MVA: " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " line on the bushings on its cover, " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " out low on its back.",

				"GAS PLANT\n\nSeparator gas made into PIPELINE GAS and LPG, each part its own skid joined by steel pipe, in at the front, out at the back:\n\nGAS COMPRESSOR (" + Math.round(Tuning.GAS_COMPRESSOR_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " three-phase: MV cable to the box on its motor's side): 125 to 1,000 psi. TEG DEHYDRATOR: dries it (no power). NGL CHILLER: chills it to -20 F; it needs a REFRIGERATION COMPRESSOR (" + Math.round(Tuning.REFRIGERATION_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ") set against its skid. Wet gas in a chiller freezes: HYDRATES.\n\n"
						+ "Out of the chiller: PIPELINE GAS (upper) for the steam plant and gas engines, and RAW NGL (lower) to the STABILIZER, a 12 m column: LPG off its east side to an LPG BULLET, NATURAL GASOLINE off its south side to a stock tank. Its reboiler burns gas or LPG piped to the west side of its base, or else some of its own LPG. A FLARE takes the gas nobody uses.",

				"SALES LINE\n\nA transmission line off the map carries PIPELINE GAS anywhere in the dimension. A RECEIPT station puts it on; a DELIVERY station anywhere else takes it off. The line keeps " + Math.round(Tuning.SALES_FUEL_RETENTION * 100) + " % as compressor fuel and never gives out more than it took in. Each station: the METER BUILDING (" + Math.round(Tuning.METER_BUILDING_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.LOW.label() + ", box on its west), an ULTRASONIC METER RUN against it and a PIPELINE TAP against the run. Sneak and right-click the building for RECEIPT or DELIVERY.\n\n"
						+ "Receipt: a FILTER SEPARATOR against the run, gas in on its north side, up to " + Math.round(Tuning.SALES_STATION_M3S) + " m3/s. Only gas-plant gas: separator gas reads OFF SPEC: RICH, wet gas OFF SPEC: WATER, biogas OFF SPEC: CO2. Delivery: a REGULATOR SKID against the run, gas out of its back. No power: the RTU battery lasts 8 hours, then METER FAILED.",

				"REFINING\n\nA crude unit splits crude by boiling point. Light sweet crude gives 2% LPG, 30% GASOLINE, 14% KEROSENE, 26% DIESEL and 28% RESIDUE (fuel oil); a gas well's CONDENSATE is mostly gasoline. Each part is real size; they work by touching, and the column names what is missing.\n\n"
						+ "TOPPING UNIT (early, 1,000 bbl/day): COLUMN, a HEATER and a PUMP SKID (" + Math.round(Tuning.TOPPING_SKID_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ") against it. Crude into the skid's north end, gasoline out of its south end; kerosene, diesel and residue off the column's foot (east, south, west). Its heater burns its own LPG, then gas or residue.",

				"CRUDE UNIT\n\nThe big one: 20,000 bbl/day. The COLUMN (30 m) with the CRUDE HEATER, SIDE STRIPPERS and OVERHEAD CONDENSER against it, the CHARGE PUMP (" + Math.round(Tuning.CHARGE_PUMP_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ") against the heater, the DESALTER against the pump.\n\n"
						+ "Crude into the desalter's north end; fuel (gas or residue) into the heater's front. Gasoline and LPG off the condenser's back, kerosene and diesel off the strippers' ends, residue off the column's foot. Diesel feeds diesel gensets; residue fires the steam plant.",

				"PETROCHEMICALS\n\nPlastic comes from ethylene. The CRACKING FURNACE cracks LPG or gasoline with steam: feed in its front, fuel gas on its east side, water pipe from a pump on its west. Then the QUENCH TOWER (pyrolysis gasoline drops out: pipe it from its east side, fuel oil from its west, or its " + String.format("%,.0f", Tuning.QUENCH_BOTTOMS_L) + " L sump fills and it stops), the CRACKED GAS COMPRESSOR (" + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + "), and the COLD BOX with a refrigeration compressor against it: ETHYLENE, FUEL GAS (pipe it back to the furnace) and LPG.\n\n"
						+ "Ethylene to the POLYETHYLENE REACTOR (" + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ") with its PELLETIZER (" + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ") against it: about 12 PLASTIC SHEETS a minute into the pelletizer's bin. Empty hand, or a hopper under it.",

				"ORES\n\nReal ores lie where real ones do, richer than real (about ten times a mined grade). Mining one gives its mineral. Its tooltip gives the grade, where it is found, the tool that mines it and the plants that use it. With JEI installed, press U over it for its page.\n\n"
						+ "DESERT and BADLANDS: uranium ore in sandstone (y 0-64), borax near the surface, rock salt and potash beds below y 0. Deep everywhere (below y -40): PITCHBLENDE, the rich uranium ore. Deepslate: nickel ore, and the chromitite and PLATINUM REEF layers. Plains, swamps and beaches: SALT DOMES, columns of rock salt with a calcite cap full of native SULFUR. Beaches: heavy mineral sand (zircon). Jungle and savanna: bauxite. Mountains: tin, molybdenum and silver. Oceans: phosphate rock. Everywhere in stone: fluorspar, galena and sphalerite, graphite, spodumene, barite, magnesite, dolomite, tungsten, cobalt and manganese.\n\n"
						+ "A furnace smelts galena to LEAD, cassiterite to TIN, sphalerite to ZINC and acanthite to SILVER. The rest wait for their plants.",

				"SCINTILLOMETER\n\nFinds uranium. Right-click: it reads the gamma count rate in counts per second. Barren rock reads " + Math.round(Tuning.SCINT_BACKGROUND_CPS) + " cps; uranium within " + Tuning.SCINT_RANGE + " blocks adds to it, more the richer and the closer it is, and the meter says which way the count rises. Pitchblende you are touching reads about " + Math.round(Tuning.SCINT_CPS_PER_U3O8 * dev.wildcatter.ore.Ore.PITCHBLENDE.grade / 1000) + ",000 cps. Phosphate rock carries a little uranium too.",

				"ACID PLANT\n\nSulfuric acid from sulfur, " + Math.round(Tuning.ACID_PLANT_TPD) + " t a day. Sulfur into a hopper on the SULFUR MELTER. It melts on steam from the WASTE HEAT BOILER against it; from cold, gas or LPG on its east side. Molten sulfur to the east side of the SULFUR FURNACE's front. Against the furnace: the MAIN BLOWER (" + Math.round(Tuning.ACID_BLOWER_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ") with the DRYING TOWER against it, and the boiler at its end (water from a pump).\n\n"
						+ "Burner gas from the boiler's back to the CONVERTER's front. Against the converter: the FINAL ABSORBER (water from a pump; acid out its south side to a stock tank) and the INTERPASS ABSORBER. Without the interpass absorber it converts " + Math.round(Tuning.ACID_CONVERSION_SINGLE * 100) + " %, not 99.8 %, and the stack shows it.\n\n"
						+ "A " + Math.round(Tuning.ACID_BLOWER_WATTS / 1000) + " kW motor started across the line needs more than one " + Math.round(Tuning.GENSET_DIESEL_WATTS / 1000) + " kW diesel set: parallel two.",

				"ACID PLANT STEAM\n\nThe waste heat boiler raises about " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.AcidSteam.boilerKgs()) + " kg/s of 40 bar steam; the melter takes a little. Pipe the boiler's top to the west side of an ACID SUPERHEATER set against the converter: the converter's heat takes it to 400 C. The 5 MW STEAM TURBINE against the superheater, with its GENERATOR, AIR-COOLED CONDENSER and a FEED PUMP against the waste heat boiler (it returns the condensate), makes about " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.AcidSteam.turbineWatts(dev.wildcatter.fluid.AcidSteam.turbineKgs()) / 1e6) + " MW.\n\n"
						+ "Through the generator breaker and a UNIT AUX TRANSFORMER onto the plant's " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " bus it carries the blower: start on gensets, then trip them. If the converter stops, the steam is wet and the turbine trips on LOW STEAM TEMPERATURE.",

				"URANIUM MILL\n\nORE into a hopper on the JAW CRUSHER, against the SAG MILL (" + Math.round(Tuning.SAG_MILL_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + "; water from a pump). Ore slurry to the LEACH TANK: acid on its east side, PYROLUSITE in a hopper on top. Leach slurry to the CCD THICKENER (water from a pump): pregnant liquor out, tailings counted.\n\n"
						+ "Liquor to the SX CIRCUIT: KEROSENE on its east side fills its settlers (" + Math.round(Tuning.SX_KEROSENE_CHARGE) + " L), ROCK SALT in a hopper. Strip liquor to the PRECIPITATION TANK, MAGNESIA in a hopper (smelt magnesite). Against it the YELLOWCAKE DRYER (gas or LPG on its east side) and the DRUM FILLER: EMPTY DRUMS in a hopper on top, YELLOWCAKE DRUMS out to a hopper under it.\n\n"
						+ "Small motors at " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ". The SAG mill is a big motor: start it on a strong supply (three diesel sets in parallel will do).",

				"YELLOWCAKE\n\nA drum holds " + Math.round(Tuning.DRUM_NET_KG) + " kg of concentrate at " + Math.round(Tuning.YELLOWCAKE_U3O8 * 100) + " % U3O8. The mill takes " + Math.round(Tuning.MILL_RECOVERY * 100) + " % of the uranium in its ore: a uranium ore block gives about 43 kg of U3O8, so about 7 and a half blocks fill a drum. At full rate (" + String.format("%.1f", Tuning.MILL_ORE_KGS) + " kg of ore a second) it fills about 4 drums an hour.\n\n"
						+ "PITCHBLENDE is rich, but the mill feeds no more than its SX circuit can take: it runs slower on pitchblende and makes the same yellowcake an hour. It saves digging, not time.",

				"ADU AND THE CALCINER\n\nThe purer route. Pipe LIQUID AMMONIA (from the ammonia plant's bullet) to the east side of the PRECIPITATION TANK: it precipitates ammonium diuranate instead of using magnesia, " + String.format("%.1f", Tuning.ADU_NH3_PER_U3O8) + " kg of ammonia a kg of U3O8. Set a URANIUM CALCINER against the tank and the drum filler, where the dryer stands: gas or LPG on its east side, its drive on " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ", its box on the north face of its corner. From cold it takes " + Math.round(Tuning.CALCINER_WARMUP_SECONDS / 60) + " minutes to reach 750 C.\n\n"
						+ "Its drums hold U3O8 at " + Math.round(Tuning.ADU_U3O8 * 100) + " %: " + Math.round(Tuning.DRUM_NET_KG * Tuning.ADU_U3O8 * dev.wildcatter.ore.Ore.U_IN_U3O8) + " kg of uranium against " + Math.round(Tuning.DRUM_NET_KG * Tuning.YELLOWCAKE_U3O8 * dev.wildcatter.ore.Ore.U_IN_U3O8) + " in a magnesia drum. In conversion they need a third less hydrogen, no HF for magnesia, and leave far less ash. One ammonia plant feeds about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.AmmoniaPlant.ammoniaKgh() / Tuning.ADU_NH3_PER_U3O8) + " kg of U3O8 an hour: a whole ISR wellfield, but a small share of a mill at full rate. Without ammonia the tank goes back to magnesia.",

				"GAMMA LOG\n\nUnder deserts and badlands lie ROLL-FRONTS: crescent bands of uranium in sandstone, about y -10 to -50, too deep for the scintillometer. Find them by drilling. A rig whose hole passes through one completes it as an ISR WELL and reports a GAMMA LOG: the ore's depth, thickness, grade (eU3O8) and GT (grade x thickness). GT " + Tuning.GAMMA_CUTOFF_GT + " or more is ORE. A hole that misses logs background.\n\n"
						+ "The band is richest along its middle (" + Math.round(Tuning.ROLL_PEAK_GRADE * 1000) / 10.0 + " %) and poorer at its edges: log a few holes to find the middle.",

				"ISR WELLFIELD\n\nNo digging: wells sweep the uranium out of the front with oxygenated water. A 5-SPOT is four injectors round one producer, within " + Tuning.ISR_PATTERN_RANGE + " blocks of it. Click a SUBMERSIBLE PUMP into a well to make it a producer; a well without one is an injector.\n\n"
						+ "Pipe the producers to the west side of the HEADER HOUSE (" + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + "; it runs their pumps, up to " + Tuning.HEADER_HOUSE_PRODUCERS + ") and its east side to the injectors. The OXYGEN GENERATOR goes against it. From its back, pipes to and from the IX COLUMNS: rock salt in a hopper, acid on their east side. Their ELUATE goes to the mill's PRECIPITATION TANK.\n\n"
						+ "A full pattern makes about " + String.format("%.1f", Tuning.ISR_PRODUCER_LPS * Tuning.ISR_HEAD_GRADE_MG_L * 3.6e-3) + " kg of U3O8 an hour; six fill a drum in about 12 hours.",

				"ISR: CO2, BLEED, SATELLITES\n\nCO2: set a CO2 LIQUEFIER against a lime kiln (its " + Math.round(Tuning.CO2_LIQUEFIER_WATTS / 1000) + " kW on " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ", box west); pipe its back to a CO2 STORAGE TANK set against the header house. The house doses its injection at 0.5 g/L and the producers' head grade rises up to " + Math.round((Tuning.CO2_HEAD_FACTOR - 1) * 100) + " %. An empty tank reads NO CO2.\n\n"
						+ "BLEED: pipe the header house's back, one block up, to an INJECTION PUMP and a disposal well. Unpiped, the bleed is only counted.\n\n"
						+ "SATELLITES: sneak-click IX columns for SATELLITE: they load but do not elute, and fill a RESIN TRAILER set against them (" + Math.round(Tuning.RESIN_TRAILER_U3O8_KG) + " kg of U3O8). Break it to carry it, loading and all; set it against the central plant's columns (ELUTION) and they take its resin and send it back eluted.",

				"CONVERSION\n\nYellowcake becomes UF6 in a line of parts, each against the next: REDUCTION REACTOR (yellowcake drums in a hopper on top, empty drums out a hopper under it; HYDROGEN on its east side), HYDROFLUORINATOR (ANHYDROUS HF east), FLUORINATOR (FLUORINE east), COLD TRAPS, DISTILLATION COLUMNS, and the CYLINDER FILLER (empty 48Y cylinders in on top, full ones out under it). The last three run on " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ".\n\n"
						+ "Hydrogen: a STEAM REFORMER on gas or LPG and pumped water. HF: the HF KILN (fluorspar in a hopper, acid and fuel on its east side) with the HF COLUMN against it. A 48Y holds " + String.format("%,.0f", Tuning.CYLINDER_48Y_KG) + " kg of UF6: about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Conversion.hoursPerCylinder()) + " hours of the plant.",

				"AMMONIA PLANT\n\nFor blasting. A STEAM REFORMER's hydrogen and a NITROGEN GENERATOR's nitrogen (PSA, " + Math.round(Tuning.N2_GENERATOR_WATTS / 1000) + " kW) both piped to the east side of the SYNGAS COMPRESSOR (" + Math.round(Tuning.SYNGAS_COMPRESSOR_WATTS / 1000) + " kW). The AMMONIA CONVERTER against it (" + Math.round(Tuning.AMMONIA_CONVERTER_WATTS / 1000) + " kW) makes " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.AmmoniaPlant.ammoniaKgh()) + " kg/h of liquid ammonia out its south side: store it in a pressure BULLET, never a stock tank. All motors " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ", boxes on the west.\n\n"
						+ "NITRIC ACID UNIT (" + Math.round(Tuning.NITRIC_UNIT_WATTS / 1000) + " kW): ammonia on its east side, water from a pump, a GAUZE PACK in a hopper on top or clicked in; 60 % acid out its south side. The gauze slowly loses platinum and is changed when worn.",

				"AMMONIUM NITRATE AND EMULSION\n\nThe NEUTRALISER takes ammonia and nitric acid on its east side and makes " + Math.round(Tuning.AN_STRENGTH * 100) + " % AN solution out its south side, by its own heat: no power. Pipe it both, from one bullet: the acid unit burns about half the ammonia and the neutraliser takes the rest, " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.AmmoniaPlant.anKgh()) + " kg/h of AN.\n\n"
						+ "The EMULSION BLENDER (" + String.format("%.1f", Tuning.EMULSION_BLENDER_WATTS / 1000) + " kW): AN solution and DIESEL on its east side, EMULSIFIER PAILS in a hopper on top, water from a pump. About " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.AmmoniaPlant.matrixKgh()) + " kg/h of EMULSION MATRIX out its back to a stock tank. Matrix is not an explosive until it is gassed in the hole: a spill or a fire does not set it off.",

				"CONVERSION'S BY-PRODUCTS\n\nCATHODE HYDROGEN: each F2 at the cells' anodes comes with an H2 at their cathodes, about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Conversion.fluorineKgs() * dev.wildcatter.block.FluorineCellHouseBlockEntity.cathodeM3PerF2() * 3600) + " Nm3/h at full current, enough for the reduction reactor. Set a CATHODE GAS SCRUBBER against the cell house (its box on the north) and pipe its back to the reducer: the reformer is then needed only to start. Without one the hydrogen is vented.\n\n"
						+ "ASH BED: the fluorinator's bed fills with ash. Sneak-click it (or a PLC's RETIRE BED) to retire it: ten minutes stopped, the ash into empty drums from a hopper on top, " + Math.round(Tuning.BED_FLUORSPAR_KG) + " kg of fluorspar for the new bed. Ash drums hold about " + Math.round(Tuning.ASH_U_SHARE * 100) + " % uranium: a uranium mill's leach tank takes them by hopper. With the world rule fluorinatorAshBed, a full bed (" + Math.round(Tuning.ASH_BED_KG / 1000) + " t) stops the fluorinator.",

				"KOH SCRUBBER\n\nSet it against the hydrofluorinator to scrub its excess HF. Its first charge of " + Math.round(Tuning.KOH_CHARGE_KG) + " kg of KOH comes as CAUSTIC POTASH on the north face of its front: a chlor-alkali cell given POTASH instead of rock salt makes it. QUICKLIME BAGS in a hopper on top regenerate the liquor, and the CaF2 comes out under it as SYNTHETIC FLUORSPAR, which the HF kiln takes. Without lime its KOH is spent in about a day: SPENT, and the hydrofluorinator stops. A hydrofluorinator with no scrubber runs as before.",

				"SUBMERGED ARC FURNACE\n\nFerroalloys. The FURNACE TRANSFORMER (" + Math.round(Tuning.FURNACE_TRANSFORMER_VA / 1e6) + " MVA) takes " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " on its west box; the FURNACE goes against its east face. At full tap it draws " + Math.round(Tuning.SAF_WATTS / 1e6) + " MW at PF " + String.format("%.2f", Tuning.SAF_POWER_FACTOR) + ": a substation's or a big turbine's load. Sneak-click the transformer to step its tap (" + Tuning.FURNACE_TAPS + " steps).\n\n"
						+ "A hopper on top feeds each bin: chromitite, quartz and coke for FERROCHROME; manganese ore, limestone and coke for FERROMANGANESE; quartz, coke and iron for FERROSILICON. Sneak-click the furnace to change; the hearth runs out first, an hour.",

				"TAPPING AND PASTE\n\nThe furnace taps every 2 hours, or when its hearth is full, out of its east face: set a BAGGING STATION there with empty bulk bags. Slag is counted.\n\n"
						+ "Its electrodes burn " + Math.round(Tuning.SAF_PASTE_KG_PER_T) + " kg of paste a tonne: feed GREEN ANODES from the anode plant. Without them the electrodes burn short, ELECTRODES SHORT, and the power halves. Four hours without power and the hearth freezes: dig the furnace out.",

				"CAPACITOR BANKS\n\nA low power factor load draws vars as well as watts: the furnace's " + Math.round(Tuning.SAF_WATTS / 1e6) + " MW at PF 0.80 is " + Math.round(Tuning.SAF_WATTS / 1e6 / Tuning.SAF_POWER_FACTOR) + " MVA, and the generators and lines carry it all.\n\n"
						+ "A CAPACITOR BANK (" + Math.round(Tuning.CAP_BANK_VAR / 1e6) + " Mvar, " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + ", box west) gives vars back. Set against the furnace transformer and wired to its bus, it lifts the feeder to about PF 0.94; the transformer reads both. It works on any bus. Sneak-click opens or closes its breaker.",

				"MOLY ROASTER AND VESSEL\n\nThe MOLY ROASTER takes thickened flotation concentrate (from Tailings' concentrator) on its east side: molybdenite is roasted to MOLY OXIDE bags, scheelite dried to SCHEELITE CONCENTRATE bags. Its SO2 goes out its south side as burner gas: pipe it to an acid plant's converter, or it stops.\n\n"
						+ "The ALUMINOTHERMIC VESSEL: a bag, iron and aluminium ingots by hopper; sneak-click fires it, 10 minutes, to FERROMOLYBDENUM or FERROTUNGSTEN. Keep out from under its hood.",

				"PHOSPHORIC ACID\n\nPHOSPHATE ROCK in a hopper on the PHOSPHATE MILL (" + Math.round(Tuning.PHOSPHATE_MILL_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + "), water from a pump: rock slurry out its south side to the north side of the PHOSPHORIC REACTOR (" + Math.round(Tuning.PHOSPHORIC_REACTOR_WATTS / 1000) + " kW). Sulfuric acid to the reactor's south side, about a third of an acid plant. The TILTING PAN FILTER goes against the reactor's east side (" + Math.round(Tuning.PAN_FILTER_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ", water from a pump): FILTER ACID out its south end, GYPSUM out the west side of its back end.\n\n"
						+ "Pipe the gypsum to a lined TAILINGS CELL: about " + Math.round(Tuning.GYPSUM_PER_P2O5 * Tuning.P2O5_TPD) + " t a day. With the cell full or broken the filter reads NO GYPSUM STACK and the plant stops. The ACID EVAPORATOR (" + Math.round(Tuning.ACID_EVAPORATOR_WATTS / 1000) + " kW) takes filter acid on its north side and process steam on its east and makes " + Math.round(Tuning.MERCHANT_ACID_P2O5 * 100) + " % MERCHANT ACID out its south side: " + Math.round(Tuning.P2O5_TPD) + " t of P2O5 a day.",

				"FERTILIZER\n\nThe GRANULATION PLANT (" + Math.round(Tuning.GRANULATION_WATTS / 1000) + " kW) takes everything on its east side: merchant acid, gas or LPG for its dryer, and rock slurry for TSP or ammonia for DAP. Sneak-click it to switch. A BAGGING STATION against it fills 1 t bags. TSP runs about " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Phosphate.tspKgs() * 3.6) + " t/h; the ammonia plant makes only " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Phosphate.dapFromAmmoniaKgh()) + " kg of DAP an hour.\n\n"
						+ "POTASH: ore in a hopper on the POTASH DISSOLVER, water from a pump, process steam on its south side, salt tails out its west side to a tailings cell. The VACUUM CRYSTALLIZER against it (steam on its south side), the POTASH DRYER against that (gas on its south side), a bagging station against the dryer: " + Math.round(Tuning.MOP_TPH) + " t/h of MOP. All " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ".",

				"URANIUM FROM PHOSPHATE\n\nPhosphate rock carries uranium, and most of it goes into the filter acid: about " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Phosphate.uraniumGPerL()) + " g a litre. Pipe the filter acid to the north side of the ACID PRETREATMENT (" + Math.round(Tuning.ACID_PRETREATMENT_WATTS / 1000) + " kW) with the DEPA-TOPO CIRCUIT (" + Math.round(Tuning.DEPA_TOPO_WATTS / 1000) + " kW) against its east side; the circuit's TREATED ACID goes from its south side to the evaporator.\n\n"
						+ "First charge: " + String.format("%,.0f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Phosphate.chargeKeroseneL()) + " L of KEROSENE on its north side and " + dev.wildcatter.fluid.Phosphate.chargeDrums() + " EXTRACTANT DRUMS in a hopper on top, then one more for make-up. IRON INGOTS in the same hopper feed the strip. About " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Phosphate.uraniumKgh()) + " kg of uranium an hour. The second cycle is not built yet: the strip holds what it takes, and when it is full the acid goes round it.",

				"FLUORINE CELLS\n\nThe CELL HOUSE holds " + Tuning.F2_CELLS + " cells in series, each " + Tuning.F2_CELL_VOLTS + " V at " + Tuning.F2_CELL_KA + " kA of DC: anhydrous HF in its front, fluorine out its back, pumped cooling water. The RECTIFIER against it turns " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " three-phase into that DC: about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Conversion.acWatts() / 1000) + " kW, a big steady load.\n\n"
						+ "Bring your generators on line before the cells: a lone " + Math.round(Tuning.GENSET_DIESEL_WATTS / 1000) + " kW diesel set cannot carry them and trips. The rectifier does not back off: if the supply sags, the fluorine slows with it. To set the cell house away from its rectifier, see DC: RECTIFIERS AND BUS BARS.",

				"CENTRIFUGE CASCADE\n\nOne steel pipe, the HEADER, joins everything: the FEED STATION (a 48Y of natural UF6 in a hopper on top; the header off its back), the PRODUCT TAKE-OFF (empty 30Bs on top) and the TAILS TAKE-OFF (empty 48Ys on top; the header into their fronts), the FREQUENCY CONVERTER (the header off its back) and the CENTRIFUGES, each joined by the top of the machine. Full and emptied cylinders drop into hoppers under the stations.\n\n"
						+ "A cascade needs a machine for each of its " + dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.stages() + " stages; more machines make it faster. A converter drives up to " + Tuning.CONVERTER_MACHINES + " on " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + ", " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.machineWatts() / 1000) + " kW a machine at " + String.format("%,.0f", Tuning.CENTRIFUGE_HERTZ) + " Hz: the smallest cascade wants a gas turbine. The stations run on " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ". Without both take-offs ready the cascade idles on TOTAL REFLUX.",

				"ZIRCONIUM\n\nZircon becomes Zircaloy-4 tube in a line of parts, each against the next: MINERAL SEPARATOR (heavy mineral sand in a hopper on top), CHLORINATOR (coal on top, CHLORINE on its east side), HAFNIUM COLUMN, KROLL REACTOR, VACUUM DISTILLATION, VAR FURNACE (tin, iron and chromite on top), EXTRUSION PRESS (" + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + "), PILGER MILL and the VACUUM ANNEAL FURNACE, whose finished tubes drop into a hopper under it. The rest run on " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ". A hopper on the chlorinator also takes another mod's ZIRCON CONCENTRATE: then it needs no separator.\n\n"
						+ "The line makes " + Math.round(Tuning.ZR_LINE_KGS * 3600) + " kg of Zircaloy an hour: an assembly's 264 cladding tubes and 25 guide thimbles in about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Zirconium.hoursPerAssembly()) + " hours. Sneak-click the pilger mill to change its dies between cladding and thimbles.",

				"CHLORINE AND MAGNESIUM\n\nThe Kroll reactor needs magnesium. The MAGNESIUM CELL goes against it and the vacuum distillation: it takes back their MgCl2 and Mg and splits the MgCl2 into magnesium and chlorine, " + Math.round(Tuning.MG_CELL_KA) + " kA from a RECTIFIER against it. Start it with the MAGNESIA CHLORINATOR against the cell (magnesia and coal on top).\n\n"
						+ "Half the chlorine leaves with the silicon as SiCl4. The CHLOR-ALKALI CELL makes it up from rock salt and pumped water, on its own rectifier: about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Zirconium.chlorAlkaliKgs() * 3600) + " kg of chlorine an hour, and hydrogen. Pipe both cells' chlorine to both chlorinators. Its CAUSTIC SODA (32 %) comes out of the west side at its back end: pipe it to a tank or the Bayer refinery's evaporator, or the cell stops. (DC: RECTIFIERS AND BUS BARS tells how to wire a cell from further away.)",

				"BATCHES, SCRAP AND HAFNIUM\n\nWith the world rule zirconiumBatches (on in new worlds) the KROLL REACTOR holds two retorts. One in the furnace takes " + Math.round(Tuning.KROLL_BATCH_KG) + " kg as the ZrCl4 comes and reduces it for " + Math.round(Tuning.KROLL_REDUCTION_S / 3600) + " hours; then it goes to the VACUUM DISTILLATION for " + Math.round(Tuning.KROLL_DISTILLATION_S / 3600) + " hours while the other is charged. The VAR FURNACE melts " + Math.round(Tuning.VAR_INGOT_KG) + " kg ingots twice, an hour a melt. The world's time scale shortens these waits.\n\n"
						+ "The press loses " + Math.round(Tuning.ZR_LOSS_EXTRUSION * 100) + " % of the metal, the pilger mill " + Math.round(Tuning.ZR_LOSS_PILGER * 100) + " % and inspection " + Math.round(Tuning.ZR_LOSS_INSPECTION * 100) + " %: " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Zirconium.lineYield() * 100) + " % reaches a tube. The pilger mill bins it as ZIRCALOY SCRAP (" + Math.round(Tuning.ZR_SCRAP_KG) + " kg) into a hopper under it; the VAR furnace takes scrap by hopper, up to " + Math.round(Tuning.VAR_SCRAP_SHARE * 100) + " % of an ingot.\n\n"
						+ "HAFNIUM: the hafnium column drops a HfCl4 DRUM (" + Math.round(Tuning.HFCL4_DRUM_HF_KG) + " kg of Hf, about " + Math.round(Tuning.HFCL4_DRUM_HF_KG / dev.wildcatter.fluid.Zirconium.hafniumKgh()) + " hours of the line) into a hopper under it. Sneak-click the Kroll reactor for a HAFNIUM CAMPAIGN: drums in a hopper on top; the stages after it follow, the VAR melts it unalloyed, and the pilger mill's fourth dies roll HAFNIUM RODLETS (" + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Zirconium.hafniumRodletKg()) + " kg). " + Tuning.HF_RODLETS_PER_RCCA + " make a hafnium RCCA.",

				"SILICA, MAGNESIUM AND CHROMIUM\n\nFUMED SILICA BURNER: set it against the chlorinator's east side (leave a cell of it for the chlorine). Hydrogen on its east side at the bottom, OXYGEN one up; it burns the SiCl4 to fumed silica sacks (a hopper under it) and 32 % HYDROCHLORIC ACID out of its back. Box on its north face.\n\n"
						+ "PIDGEON FURNACE: dolomite in a LIME KILN burns to DOLIME bags. Dolime, ferrosilicon and fluorspar in a hopper on top, gas on its east side: " + Math.round(Tuning.PIDGEON_MG_KGS * 3600) + " kg of magnesium an hour, cast into ingots at the end of each " + Math.round(Tuning.PIDGEON_CYCLE_S / 3600) + "-hour cycle. A hopper on the MAGNESIUM CELL takes them.\n\n"
						+ "CHROMATE KILN: chromite and sulfur on top, caustic soda on its north end, gas on its east side: a " + Math.round(Tuning.CR2O3_SACK_KG) + " kg sack of CHROMIC OXIDE an hour. Broken while it holds chromate it spills poison. " + Tuning.VESSEL_CR_SACKS + " sacks and " + Tuning.VESSEL_CR_ALUMINIUM + " aluminium ingots fire in the aluminothermic vessel to CHROMIUM METAL, which the VAR furnace takes in place of chromite.",

				"ALUMINA: THE BAYER PROCESS\n\nBauxite becomes alumina in a line joined by steel pipe, each part's inlet at its front (north) and outlet at its back: BALL MILL (bauxite on top, strong liquor in), DIGESTER (PROCESS STEAM on its east side) set against the FLASH TANKS, SETTLER, POLISHING FILTERS, PRECIPITATOR, HYDRATE FILTER. The settler's red mud leaves its east side for the MUD WASHER (pumped water) and the RESIDUE FILTER PRESS, which drops RED MUD blocks into a hopper under it for a dry stack.\n\n"
						+ "Set the CALCINER (gas on its east side; its fan on " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ") against the hydrate filter, and a BAGGING STATION (empty bulk bags on top) against the calciner: alumina comes out in 1 t bags. Sneak-click the hydrate filter to send some hydrate to a bagging station set against it.\n\n"
						+ "The hydrate filter's SPENT LIQUOR goes to the EVAPORATOR (steam, and 32 % caustic on its own run, on its east side), set against the CAUSTICIZER (quicklime bags on top). Its STRONG LIQUOR goes back to the ball mill. A PACKAGE BOILER (gas, pumped water) makes the steam.\n\n"
						+ "Full rate: " + Math.round(Tuning.BAYER_ALUMINA_KGS * 86.4) + " t of alumina a day, a bauxite block about every " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Bayer.aluminaPerBauxiteBlock() / Tuning.BAYER_ALUMINA_KGS / 60) + " minutes. It needs about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Bayer.caustic() * Tuning.BAYER_ALUMINA_KGS * 3600) + " kg of caustic an hour (about 11 chlor-alkali cells) and " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Bayer.lime() * Tuning.BAYER_ALUMINA_KGS * 3600) + " kg of lime. Short of either, the evaporator and then the whole plant slow down. The evaporator starts with " + Math.round(Tuning.BAYER_LIQUOR_CHARGE_SECONDS / 60) + " minutes of liquor in its storage.",

				"LIME, ALF3 AND CHLORINE\n\nLIMESTONE is found in thick beds under plains, forests and rivers. The LIME KILN (limestone on top, gas on its east side) burns it to quicklime; set a BAGGING STATION against it for quicklime bags, the causticizer's feed.\n\n"
						+ "The AlF3 REACTOR (hydrate bags on top; ANHYDROUS HF from an HF column and gas on its east side, each on its own run) makes " + Math.round(Tuning.ALF3_KGS * 3600) + " kg of aluminium fluoride an hour for the potline's bath. A bagging station against it fills AlF3 bags.\n\n"
						+ "Making caustic also makes chlorine. The CHLORINE FILLER (chlorine pipe at its front, empty ton containers on top) liquefies it into " + Math.round(Tuning.CL2_TON_KG) + " kg ton containers, which drop into a hopper under it.",

				"PETROLEUM COKE AND PITCH\n\nThe DELAYED COKER takes RESIDUE at the COKER FRACTIONATOR's front. The COKER HEATER (gas, coker gas or LPG on its east side) is set against the fractionator and two COKE DRUMS, which stand on the COKE PIT (" + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ", pumped cutting water). " + Math.round(Tuning.COKER_COKE_YIELD * 100) + " % of the residue stays in the drums as coke; the rest comes back to the fractionator as gas oil (the diesel line, its back at x 0), naphtha (the gasoline line, at x 2) and COKER GAS (its east side), which the plant's burners fire on. The pit cuts the coke out of the drum that is not filling and drops GREEN PETROLEUM COKE into a hopper under it.\n\n"
						+ "The COKE KILN (green coke on top, fuel on its east side) calcines it to " + Math.round(Tuning.COKE_CALCINE_YIELD * 100) + " % of its weight; set it against the COKE COOLER, and a bagging station against the cooler for calcined coke bags.\n\n"
						+ "Pitch comes from coal. The COAL TOWER (coal or coal blocks on top) feeds the COKE OVEN BATTERY, with the PUSHER MACHINE on its west side and the COKE QUENCH TOWER (pumped water) on its east. Its raw gas leaves its back for the BY-PRODUCT PLANT (" + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + "), which sends out COKE OVEN GAS (burners, gas engines and gas turbines take it, and coker gas) and COAL TAR. The TAR STILL (fuel on its east side) makes PITCH (its back at x 0) and tar oils (at x 2). METALLURGICAL COKE drops under the quench tower; it works wherever coal does.",

				"ANODES\n\nThe ANODE PASTE PLANT (" + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + "; calcined coke bags and crushed butts on top, PITCH on its east side) mixes paste of " + Math.round(Tuning.PASTE_COKE * 100) + " % coke, " + Math.round(Tuning.PASTE_BUTTS * 100) + " % butts and " + Math.round(Tuning.PASTE_PITCH * 100) + " % pitch. With no butts it makes them up with coke. The FORMING PRESS against it presses a " + Math.round(Tuning.GREEN_ANODE_KG) + " kg GREEN ANODE.\n\n"
						+ "The RING BAKING FURNACE (green anodes on top, fuel on its east side) bakes them to BAKED ANODES. The RODDING SHOP (baked anodes, ANODE RODS, iron ingots and SPENT ANODES on top) casts each anode onto a rod with an iron ingot's thimbles, and strips spent anodes into their rod, which goes back on its line, and CRUSHED BUTTS for the paste plant. An anode rod is three copper ingots over a steel ingot.\n\n"
						+ "The plant is sized for " + Math.round(Tuning.ANODES_PER_SECOND * 86400) + " anodes a day: enough for a 40-pot line.",

				"THE POTLINE\n\nRECTIFORMERS take " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " at the west side of their front corner and give DC, + over - on their east side. Set side by side they form a yard that holds one line current (sneak and right-click: " + Math.round(Tuning.POTLINE_SETPOINTS_KA[0]) + " to " + Math.round(Tuning.POTLINE_SETPOINTS_KA[Tuning.POTLINE_SETPOINTS_KA.length - 1]) + " kA), shared among the units online, at most " + Math.round(Tuning.RECTIFORMER_AMPS / 1000) + " kA each, up to " + Math.round(Tuning.RECTIFORMER_MAX_DC_VOLTS) + " V. Four carry a line, one a spare.\n\n"
						+ "POTS set side by side join through their risers: + on the west side, - on the east, low down in the middle. Run 180 kA BUS (aluminium, or copper for the first line) from the yard's + to a row's first pot, from its last pot to the next row, and back to the yard's -. A pot is about " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Potline.potVolts()) + " V.\n\n"
						+ "A pot's hopper on top takes alumina bags (reacted ones first), AlF3 bags and RODDED ANODES. It makes about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Potline.aluminiumKgs(Tuning.POT_AMPS, Tuning.POT_CURRENT_EFFICIENCY) * 3600) + " kg of aluminium an hour, and changes an anode every " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Potline.anodeLifeDays() * 24 / Tuning.POT_ANODES) + " h, dropping the SPENT ANODE below. With no rodded anode the change is OVERDUE, and the pot makes less.\n\n"
						+ "With its alumina gone it has an ANODE EFFECT: about " + Math.round(Tuning.POT_AE_VOLTS) + " V, no metal, and CF4. Below " + Math.round(Tuning.POT_FREEZE_AMPS / 1000) + " kA for " + Math.round(Tuning.POT_FREEZE_SECONDS / 3600) + " h it FREEZES and opens the line. Sneak and right-click a pot to CUT IT OUT: its shorting bars carry the line past it, live. Break a frozen pot for its SPENT POT LINING.\n\n"
						+ "Each pot's AUXILIARIES (its controller, feeders, crust breakers and beam jacks) take " + Math.round(Tuning.POT_AUX_WATTS / 1000) + " kW at " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " on the front of its main cell: run a cable along the row's front. Without it the feeders stop and the pot runs on the " + Math.round(Tuning.POT_BATH_ALUMINA_KG) + " kg of alumina in its bath, then has an anode effect.\n\n"
						+ "The row's duct runs along the pots' tops. Pipe POT GAS from a row's end to the FUME TREATMENT CENTRE's west side; with a MAIN FAN (" + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ") against it, it turns fresh alumina bags into reacted ones, and the pots need " + Math.round(Tuning.POT_ALF3_TREATED * 1000) + " kg of AlF3 a t instead of " + Math.round(Tuning.POT_ALF3_VENTED * 1000) + ".",

				"TAPPING AND CASTING\n\nA pot holds about two days of metal, " + String.format("%,.0f", Tuning.POT_METAL_HOLD_KG) + " kg; then it reads FULL: TAP IT. Right-click it with the TAPPING CRUCIBLE (up to " + String.format("%,.0f", Tuning.CRUCIBLE_KG) + " kg), then right-click the INGOT CASTING MACHINE (" + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ") to pour. It casts " + Math.round(Tuning.CASTER_KGS * 3.6) + " t an hour into " + Tuning.AL_INGOT_KG + " kg ALUMINIUM INGOTS, out to a hopper under it.\n\n"
						+ "Nine ingots make a BLOCK OF ALUMINIUM; seven blocks over two bricks make a metre of 180 kA aluminium bus. Two ingots over a steel ingot make an ANODE ROD.",

				"BLUEPRINTS\n\nA BLUEPRINT holds a plant: every block and true-size part in a box, with their facings and cable sizes. Sneak-right-click a blank one in the air to step through the LIBRARY of the mod's plants, from the steam plant to the potline.\n\n"
						+ "The SURVEY TOOL records your own: right-click two corners, then right-click again with a blueprint in your off hand. Sneak-right-click clears the corners.\n\n"
						+ "Held, a blueprint shows its ghost where it would stand, turned the way you face: parts as boxes (red where something is in the way), blocks as coloured cubes. Right-click a block to set its SITE MARKER; the marker keeps the ghost up for everyone until the plant stands, and its readout names the next lift and its mass. Build it by hand, or with a crane. Sneak-right-click the marker to switch its site between BUILD and DISMANTLE: every crane on it follows.",

				"CRANES\n\nA crane builds the site marker nearest it, lift by lift in the marker's order, from a CHEST, BARREL or HOPPER against its base, at its real speeds. A lift it cannot make it passes over, but never onto one resting on a lift not yet set. Each lift: the riggers sling it (" + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.RIG_SECONDS) + " s), it is hoisted clear of the site, slewed and moved out, lowered and set (" + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.RIG_SECONDS) + " s). Its readout names the lift, the load on the hook against its chart, and what it waits for: TOO HEAVY, OUT OF REACH, TOO HIGH, WAITING (what the chest lacks), CHEST FULL.\n\n"
						+ "The TOWER CRANE: 16 t out to 19.6 m, falling to 3 t at its 75 m jib's tip, " + dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.TOWER_HOOK_HEIGHT + " m under the hook. Feed it " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " at its switch cabinet (the west face of its corner, facing north): the hoist draws up to " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.TOWER_HOIST_WATTS / 1000) + " kW.\n\n"
						+ "The CRAWLER CRANE: up to 300 t close in on a short boom; sneak-right-click steps its boom, 20 to 95 m, between lifts: the longer the boom, the farther it reaches and the less it lifts. It runs on its own diesel engine: pipe diesel to its crawlers (a " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.CRAWLER_TANK_LITRES) + " L tank). In DISMANTLE a crane lifts the site out, last lift first, into its chest.\n\n"
						+ "WIND: rain and storms blow harder higher up. Over its limit at its jib or boom head (tower " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.TOWER_WIND_LIMIT) + " m/s, crawler " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.CRAWLER_WIND_LIMIT) + ", ring " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.RING_WIND_LIMIT) + ") a crane holds. GROUND: a crawler needs " + dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.CRAWLER_GROUND_T_M2 + " t/m2 under its tracks (gravel, rock or concrete, not dirt or sand), the ring crane " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.RING_GROUND_T_M2) + " t/m2 (rock, concrete or crane rail): SOFT GROUND. BLOCKED: a block in the jib's or boom's slew, or another tower crane's mast, stops a lift until it is cleared.",

				"HEAVY LIFTS\n\nThe RING CRANE: a 48.5 m ring with 5,200 t of counterweight, 5,000 t at 40 m on its 118 m main boom (its hook takes " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.LoadChart.RING_HOOK_SWL) + " t), out to 838 t at 170 m on the 160.5 m boom; sneak-right-click steps between them. Its chart starts 40 m out, so its chest is a LAYDOWN: the chest, barrel or hopper nearest it within its reach. Its hook block alone is " + dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.RING_HOOK_BLOCK_TONNES + " t. It slews " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.RING_SLEW_DEG_MIN) + " degrees a minute: put the laydown near the site's bearing. Twelve diesels drive it: pipe diesel to its ring (a " + String.format("%,.0f", dev.wildcatter.crane.CraneKind.RING_TANK_LITRES) + " L tank).\n\n"
						+ "RAILS: lay CRANE RAIL in a row under its middle, flush with the ground. With no lift in reach it skids along them, " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.crane.Siting.RING_TRAVEL_M_H) + " m an hour, until the nearest unfinished site is close in, and stops at a block in its path or the rails' end.\n\n"
						+ "SHARING: several cranes in reach of one marker work it together, each taking the lifts its chart holds. No lift is taken twice.\n\n"
						+ "TANDEM: a part too heavy for any one crane goes up on two. The crane with it in its chest leads; each crane carries half, and that half may use only 80 % of its chart. Both move at the slower crane's speed, and both hold if either loses power.",

				"FUEL PELLETS\n\nA line of parts, each against the next: the UF6 AUTOCLAVE (a 30B of LEU in a hopper on top, the empty out below), the IDR KILN (HYDROGEN on its east side, pumped water for steam), GRANULATOR, PELLET PRESS, SINTERING FURNACE (hydrogen on its east side: 1,750 C) and PELLET GRINDER. All run on " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ".\n\n"
						+ "A pellet is " + Tuning.PELLET_DIAMETER_MM + " mm across and " + String.format("%.2f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Fuel.pelletGrams()) + " g of UO2. The line makes about " + Math.round(Tuning.FUEL_LINE_U_KGS * 3600) + " kg of uranium an hour into pellets; a 30B lasts about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Fuel.hoursPer30b()) + " hours.",

				"FUEL RODS AND ASSEMBLY\n\nAfter the grinder: the ROD LOADER (cladding tubes and steel ingots on top) puts " + dev.wildcatter.fluid.Fuel.pelletsPerRod() + " pellets in each tube; the ROD WELDER (helium cylinders on top) fills each rod with helium at 2 MPa and welds it shut; the ASSEMBLY FIXTURE (25 guide thimbles, 6 spacer grids and steel on top) pulls 264 rods into the skeleton. The assembly drops into a hopper under it: " + String.format("%.0f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Fuel.assemblyU()) + " kg of uranium. Stand it up anywhere: it is 4 m tall.\n\n"
						+ "Helium comes from the HELIUM RECOVERY UNIT on a gas plant's pipeline gas (empty cylinders on top). Spacer grids come from the pilger mill's third die.",

				"BORIC ACID AND BORON CARBIDE\n\nThe BORAX DISSOLVER (borax on top, sulfuric acid on its east side, pumped water) and the BORIC ACID CRYSTALLIZER against it make " + Math.round(Tuning.BORIC_ACID_KGS * 3600) + " kg of boric acid an hour, in " + Math.round(Tuning.BORIC_ACID_BAG_KG) + " kg bags. The reactor's coolant carries it.\n\n"
						+ "The B4C FURNACE (boric acid and coal on top) makes boron carbide pellets, a 1 kg tray every " + Math.round(1 / Tuning.B4C_KGS / 60) + " minutes. The RCCA BENCH (9 trays and a steel ingot on top) builds a control rod cluster of 24 rodlets. The reactor takes 5.",

				"THE REACTOR CORE AND RODS\n\nThe REACTOR VESSEL holds 9 fuel assemblies and 5 RCCAs: right-click them in while it is cold, empty of pressure and its pumps are stopped. The core makes " + Math.round(Reactor.ratedWatts() / 1e6) + " MW of heat at full power. An assembly lasts about " + Math.round(Reactor.cycleHours() * 3) + " hours at full power; refuel a third of the core at a time.\n\n"
						+ "The CRDM HEAD sits on the vessel and moves the rods. The four edge rods are the shutdown bank, out before startup. The centre rod, bank D, holds the power. The CVCS SKID (boric acid bags on top, pumped water) sets the boron: sneak-click to change its target. Boron holds most of the core's reactivity; dilute it as the fuel burns.\n\n"
						+ "The REACTOR CONSOLE, against the vessel: sneak-click to step the setpoint. TRIP drops every rod in 2 s. Leave TRIP to reset once the cause has cleared.",

				"THE PRIMARY LOOP AND STARTUP\n\nEach loop is a STEAM GENERATOR against the vessel with a REACTOR COOLANT PUMP (" + Math.round(Tuning.RCP_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ") against it. The PRESSURIZER goes against the vessel or a steam generator. Feedwater goes in at the steam generator's bottom east side; steam comes out of its top.\n\n"
						+ "Startup: fill the RCS through the CVCS at the boron target. Heat the pressurizer to " + Tuning.RCP_SEAL_MPA + " MPa so the pumps can run. The pumps' heat brings the loop to " + Tuning.TAVG_NO_LOAD + " C in about half an hour, and the pressurizer to " + Tuning.RCS_MPA + " MPa. Set a power on the console: the shutdown bank comes out and bank D pulls to criticality, at most 1 decade a minute.\n\n"
						+ "Without a turbine, the AUX FEED PUMP feeds the steam generators and their dump valves vent the steam: about " + Math.round(Tuning.AFW_KGS / Reactor.steamPerGenerator() / 2 * 100) + " % power. Trips: high flux, low flow, pressure, overtemperature, low steam generator level, lost rod drive power.",

				"REFUELLING\n\nRefuel at cold shutdown: under 60 C, no pressure, the coolant pumps stopped. Keep the RHR running: the core still makes heat. Put the REFUELLING MACHINE against the vessel, a FUEL TRANSFER SYSTEM against the machine and the SPENT FUEL POOL's controller against that. New assemblies go in the machine's hopper.\n\n"
						+ "Sneak-click the machine: REFUEL sends the 3 most-burned assemblies to the pool, shuffles the rest and loads 3 new ones, a move a minute. DEFUEL takes the whole core out, a damaged one too, which clears the damage. Spent assemblies are never items: too radioactive to carry.",

				"THE SPENT FUEL POOL\n\nThe pool's controller digs a 6 x 6 m pool 12 m deep in front of itself, lines it and fills it. Its racks hold 36 assemblies, glowing Cherenkov blue while they are hot. Pipe circulating water to its west side for its cooling, and pump make-up water to it.\n\n"
						+ "Without cooling the pool heats and, after a day or two, boils away. As the water falls the fuel loses its shielding: with less than 3 m over it, standing at the edge becomes deadly.",

				"RADIATION AND THE DOSIMETER\n\nCarry a DOSIMETER: click it for the dose rate and your dose. In your hotbar it alarms over 1 mSv/h and over 20 mSv, a worker's year. Water and solid blocks between you and a source shield you; distance helps by its square.\n\n"
						+ "A big dose in a short time makes you sick: from 1 Sv nausea and weakness, from 3 Sv hunger and slowness too, from 6 Sv you wither, and 8 Sv kills. The body repairs: the recent dose halves each day. Sources: irradiated fuel (deadly bare), a damaged core (about 1 Sv/h close by), an operating reactor (inside its shield, mild), and uranium ore (harmless).",

				"AFTER A TRIP\n\nA tripped core still makes heat: about 6 % of full power a few seconds later, 1.2 % after an hour, 0.6 % after a day. Keep a coolant pump, the aux feed pump and the dump valves (or the turbine's steam dump) going, or the RCS heats up.\n\n"
						+ "Xenon builds after a trip and peaks about 8 hours later, worth some 4,600 pcm: a restart then needs the boron diluted, or a wait.\n\n"
						+ "To cool down, step the console to COOLDOWN: the rods stay in, the dump valves bring the temperature down and the spray brings the pressure with it. Below 177 C and 2.9 MPa the RHR PUMP (against the vessel) and the RHR HEAT EXCHANGER (against the pump, circulating water piped to its north side) take it to 50 C: cold shutdown.",

				"CORE DAMAGE\n\nIf nothing carries the decay heat away, the coolant boils off through the PORVs. Below about 60 % of its water the core uncovers and the fuel heats. Over 1,200 C the Zircaloy cladding fails: CORE DAMAGE, and the reactor will never restart until it is defuelled.\n\n"
						+ "Hot Zircaloy burns in steam and makes hydrogen. At about 18 kg in the building's air it explodes, wrecking the parts round the vessel. The vessel and its head are thick steel and stand.",

				"CONTAINMENT\n\nBuild the island inside CONTAINMENT CONCRETE: floor, walls and roof, with an EQUIPMENT HATCH (sneak-click to open or shut) and a PERSONNEL AIRLOCK (click to pass through; its doors are interlocked, so the building stays closed). A CONTAINMENT MONITOR inside, facing into the air, reads CLOSED and the free volume (up to " + String.format("%,d", (int) Tuning.CONTAINMENT_MAX_M3) + " m3), or OPEN and near where the air gets out.\n\n"
						+ "Closed, the building takes the core's hydrogen into its lower compartment. HYDROGEN RECOMBINERS work on their own above " + Math.round(Tuning.PAR_START * 100) + " %. HYDROGEN IGNITERS (glow plugs on " + Voltage.LOW.label() + ") burn it at 4 % in small burns, while powered. A compartment that reaches 4 % with no powered igniter blasts. Steam let in raises its pressure; at " + Tuning.CONTAINMENT_FAIL_FACTOR + " times its " + Tuning.CONTAINMENT_DESIGN_MPA + " MPa design the hatch fails.",

				"THE RELIEF TANK AND THE REACTOR RULES\n\nA PRESSURIZER RELIEF TANK against the pressurizer or the vessel takes what the PORVs let go into " + Math.round(Tuning.RELIEF_TANK_KG / 1000) + " m3 of water. At " + Tuning.RELIEF_DISC_MPA + " MPa its rupture disc bursts. Sneak-click: its spray (the CVCS's makeup water), or a new disc once it is under 100 C.\n\n"
						+ "World rules (/wildcatter rule): reactorLtop: the vessel's P-T curve (" + Tuning.PT_LOW_MPA + " MPa cold); sneak-click the console's lower face for LTOP ARMED (PORVs at " + Tuning.LTOP_MPA + " MPa below " + Math.round(Tuning.LTOP_ENABLE_C) + " C); over twice the curve the vessel fails. reactorHeatupLimit: HEAT-UP RATE over " + Math.round(Tuning.HEATUP_LIMIT_C_PER_H) + " C/h in plant time. reactorRealHeatup: the real 8-12 hour heat-up. reactorDeltaTTrips: the OT and OP delta-T trips.",

				"DRY CASKS\n\nOld fuel leaves the pool in a welded canister. Set the CASK LOADING STATION (" + Math.round(Tuning.CASK_STATION_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + ") against the pool's controller and put empty DRY STORAGE CANISTERS in its hopper. Build a STORAGE MODULE on a pad within " + Math.round(Tuning.CASK_LINK_BLOCKS) + " m and sneak-click the station with the Power Meter to link it.\n\n"
						+ "Sneak-click the pool's controller for LOAD CASK: the station takes the coolest assemblies, a move a minute, up to " + Tuning.CANISTER_ASSEMBLIES + " a canister, each under " + String.format("%.1f", Tuning.CANISTER_MAX_W_EACH / 1000) + " kW and " + Math.round(Tuning.CANISTER_MAX_W / 1000) + " kW in all. It dries and backfills the canister (" + Math.round(Tuning.CASK_DRY_SECONDS / 60) + " minutes), welds it (" + Math.round(Tuning.CASK_WELD_SECONDS / 60) + ") and sends it to the module (" + Math.round(Tuning.CASK_TRANSFER_SECONDS / 60) + "). The module's 1 m walls shield it; it cannot be broken while loaded.",

				"CONTROL RODS\n\nAn RCCA of B4C rodlets burns its boron-10 while it is in the core at power. With reactorRodWear on (new worlds), the vessel reads each RCCA's B-10: at " + Math.round(Tuning.B10_REPLACE * 100) + " % it reads REPLACE, and past " + Math.round(Tuning.B10_WORTH_FALL_FROM * 100) + " % its worth falls, to " + Math.round(Tuning.B10_WORTH_FLOOR * 100) + " % at " + Math.round(Tuning.B10_WORTH_FALL_TO * 100) + " %. Bank D, in at power, wears first. An RCCA taken out keeps its count.\n\n"
						+ "A HAFNIUM RCCA (24 hafnium rodlets at the RCCA bench) is worth " + Math.round(Tuning.HF_RCCA_WORTH * 100) + " % of a fresh B4C one and never wears. Load any mix. The vessel reads the SHUTDOWN MARGIN: the rods with the strongest one stuck out, less the power defect. Below " + Math.round(Tuning.SHUTDOWN_MARGIN * 1e5) + " pcm it alarms SDM LOW.\n\n"
						+ "SODIUM SULFATE: a BAGGING STATION against the borax dissolver fills 1 t bags of it. Wildcatter has no use for it: dump the bags in a lined cell (a hopper on the decant tower, or a right-click on it).",

				"CONTAMINATION AND NEW FUEL\n\nWith reactorContamination on, the coolant carries activity (the CVCS reads it; its resin takes it out). Breaking a primary part with water in it, a relief tank's disc, a damaged core, a failed hatch or a drained pool puts contamination round them: a dose source that sticks to you as you walk on it. A PERSONNEL MONITOR (" + Voltage.LOW.label() + ") reads and washes you; a DECONTAMINATION WASHER, plugged in within " + Math.round(Tuning.WASHER_REACH) + " m with a water bucket on you, cleans a block by 90 %. The Power Meter reads a block.\n\n"
						+ "The NEW-FUEL INSPECTION STAND (hopper in, hopper out) marks assemblies INSPECTED. With fuelHandlingDamage on, a move may bend a grid; the stand finds it and the ASSEMBLY FIXTURE straightens it (hopper on top). Loaded uninspected, a bent grid leaks after a third of a cycle.",

				"THE TURBINE ISLAND\n\nThe reactor's steam drives a " + Math.round(Tuning.TG60_WATTS / 1e6) + " MW turbine. In a line: the TURBINE VALVE CHEST (steam piped from the steam generators' tops onto its top), the HP TURBINE (the controller) with the MOISTURE SEPARATOR REHEATER beside it, the LP TURBINE, and the 60 MVA GENERATOR against the LP turbine, then its 3,000 A breaker, bus duct and the 60 MVA GSU.\n\n"
						+ "The MAIN CONDENSER goes against the LP turbine. CIRCULATING WATER PUMPS (" + Math.round(Tuning.CW_PUMP_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + ") must stand with their bottom 3 cells in a lake or river; pipe their water to the condenser's north side. No water, no vacuum: the turbine trips.\n\n"
						+ "The water goes back through two CONDENSATE PUMPS against the condenser, the DEAERATOR (pumped make-up water), two MAIN FEED PUMPS and the HP FEEDWATER HEATER, whose feedwater you pipe to the steam generators. Sneak-click the HP turbine to reset a trip. Above half power a turbine trip trips the reactor.",

				"THE COOLING TOWER\n\nPlace the NATURAL-DRAFT COOLING TOWER at the edge of where it will stand: the tower rises 34 m in front of it, " + Math.round(Tuning.TOWER_TOP_Y) + " m tall and about 64 m across. Feed gray concrete, steel ingots and (for the fill) plastic sheets by a hopper on top. It builds the basin and fills its pond, then the raker columns, then the shell one 1.5 m lift at a time, then the fill: about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.CoolingTower.totalConcrete()) + " concrete and " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.CoolingTower.totalSteelIngots()) + " steel ingots in all.\n\n"
						+ "Stand the circulating water pumps in its basin and pipe the condenser's warm water (its south side) to the controller's top. No fans: the warm air draws itself up the shell. The water comes back about 8 C over the air's wet-bulb temperature, worse in hot humid places. It evaporates about 42 kg/s at full load: pump make-up water to the controller.",

				"STATION SERVICE\n\nA running plant powers itself. The UNIT AUXILIARY TRANSFORMER (" + Math.round(Tuning.UAT_VA / 1e6 * 10) / 10.0 + " MVA) takes the generator bus down to " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " for the coolant, feed and circulating water pumps, and a unit substation takes that to " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " for the rest.\n\n"
						+ "To start a plant you need power from outside: a grid line through the GSU, or another generator on the bus. Start the pumps one at a time: each draws six times its current while it gets up to speed.",

				"CASCADE OPERATIONS\n\nASSAY: sneak-click the FEED STATION to step its setting: product 3.0, 3.5, 4.0, 4.5 or 4.95 %, then tails 0.20, 0.25 or 0.30 %. Lower product needs fewer stages and less work: 3.00 / 0.25 % runs on " + dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.stages(0.03, 0.0025) + " machines. Each 30B carries its assay into the fuel plant, the assembly and the reactor: 3 % fuel starts with about half the reactivity of 4.95 %.\n\n"
						+ "COOLING: a CASCADE COOLING SKID with its side on the header and circulating water on its north face cools the casings, " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.machineWatts() / (Tuning.WATER_SPECIFIC_HEAT * Tuning.CASING_RISE_C)) + " kg/s a machine. Once a cascade has had a skid it needs one: " + Math.round(Tuning.CASING_HOT_SECONDS / 60) + " minutes without cooling and it reads CASING HOT and holds its feed.\n\n"
						+ "SPIN-UP: with the world rule cascadeSpinUp, machines take " + Math.round(Tuning.SPIN_UP_SECONDS / 60) + " minutes to reach speed and coast for an hour when their drive goes, still separating as they slow.",

				"SEPARATIVE WORK\n\nA SWU measures the work of splitting uranium. Each kg of " + String.format("%.2f", Tuning.ASSAY_PRODUCT * 100) + " % product takes " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.feedPerProduct()) + " kg of natural uranium and " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.swuPerProduct()) + " SWU, and leaves " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.tailsPerProduct()) + " kg of " + String.format("%.2f", Tuning.ASSAY_TAILS * 100) + " % tails.\n\n"
						+ "A machine does " + String.format("%.1f", dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.machineSwuPerSecond() * 3600) + " SWU an hour at full speed. " + dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.stages() + " machines fill a 30B (" + String.format("%,.0f", Tuning.CYLINDER_30B_KG) + " kg of UF6) in about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.hoursPer30b(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Enrichment.stages())) + " hours and use most of what one conversion plant makes.",

				"GENSETS\n\nA genset is an engine and an alternator on one skid, built from parts you craft: an ENGINE (block casting, pistons, crankshaft, cylinder head and injectors, or spark plugs for gas) and an ALTERNATOR (stator winding, rotor field, exciter). Everything is its real size: the diesel set is 5 x 2 m and 4 m high, the gas set 7 x 2 m.\n\nPut down the base first: the SUB-BASE FUEL TANK (diesel) or the BASE FRAME (gas). Then click each part anywhere on top of it: RADIATOR, ENGINE, ALTERNATOR, CONTROL PANEL. Each goes to its own place on the skid. Click the SILENCER on top of the engine.\n\nDiesel " + Math.round(Tuning.GENSET_DIESEL_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, gas " + Math.round(Tuning.GENSET_GAS_WATTS / 1000) + " kW, both " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " three-phase. The cables connect low on the panel's end, away from the engine. Right-click the panel to start: it cranks to speed in " + (int) Tuning.GENSET_START_SECONDS + " s and closes its breaker. Diesel: a bucket on any part of the tank (1,000 L) or a pipe from a diesel tank. Gas: a pipe from a separator's gas side to any part of the engine (wet gas straight from a well will not do); pipeline gas, coke oven gas and coker gas do as well, by their heat. Coke oven gas is mostly hydrogen and knocks: on it the set is held to " + Math.round(Tuning.GENSET_GAS_WATTS * Tuning.GENSET_COKE_OVEN_GAS_DERATE / 1000) + " kW, as real coke gas engines are. A redstone signal at the panel also starts the set, and its dropping stops it: a transfer switch's engine-start contact.",

				"BIOGAS\n\nBiogas is 60 % methane and 40 % CO2, about " + Math.round(Tuning.BIOGAS_JOULES_PER_M3 / 1e6) + " MJ/m3. Another mod's digester puts it on steel pipe; Wildcatter makes none. A GAS GENSET burns it, derated to " + Math.round(Tuning.GENSET_BIOGAS_WATTS / 1000) + " kW (BIOGAS: " + Math.round(Tuning.GENSET_BIOGAS_WATTS / 1000) + " kW MAX), about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.fluid.Biogas.fullLoadM3h()) + " m3/h at full load. Asked for more it droops. A FIREBOX burns it too.\n\n"
						+ "The steam plant burner, gas turbines, reformer, dryers and the sales line need pipeline gas and refuse it. A farm digester makes little: store it and run the set in bursts on a redstone start.",
				"SUBSTATION\n\nA yard of true-size parts, 16 x 9 m, " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " side (west when facing north) first: " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " BREAKER, DISCONNECT and BUS, the POWER TRANSFORMER (" + Math.round(Tuning.SUBSTATION_VA / 1e6) + " MVA, delta to wye), then the " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " BUS, DISCONNECT and FEEDER BREAKER, with the RELAY PANEL north of the transformer. Every part's terminals sit on the yard's centre line, so placed in their spots they touch. Nothing snaps: the transformer's readout names the next part it needs and where. The transformer is energized only once the line is complete. A CHAIN-LINK FENCE with a BARBED-WIRE TOP keeps people out.\n\nThe relay panel trips both breakers on a fault: a time-overcurrent relay (51) above " + Math.round(Tuning.RELAY_51_PICKUP * 100) + " percent of full load, sooner the heavier it is, and an instantaneous one (50) at " + Math.round(Tuning.RELAY_50_MULTIPLE * 100) + " percent. Right-click the panel to reset. Open a DISCONNECT only after its breaker: under load it draws an arc that burns anyone near.\n\nA plant with no " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " yard can go straight from " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " to " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " through a " + Math.round(Tuning.STEP_UP_10_VA / 1e6) + " MVA POWER TRANSFORMER (5 m across, 4 m deep, 5 m tall): the " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " cable low on its back, the " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " to the bushings on its cover. It works either way, up or down.",

				"GENERATOR BUS PROTECTION\n\nThe " + Voltage.GENERATOR.label() + " bus duct between a generator's breaker and its transformers can have its own relays. Put a 15 KV FEEDER BREAKER on each branch off the bus (to the GSU, the UAT or a load bank): 3 m along the duct, 3 m tall; sneak-right-click sets it to 1,200, 2,000 or 3,000 A. Stand a GENERATOR BUS RELAY PANEL against the bus duct. It finds the bus up to its breakers and watches it:\n\n"
						+ "87B, BUS DIFFERENTIAL: current that goes into the bus and does not come out at a breaker is going into a fault on it. It opens every breaker on the bus at once, and the lockout (86B) holds them open until you right-click the panel.\n\n"
						+ "51V on each generator breaker: an overcurrent trip whose pickup falls as the voltage sags. 50/51 on each feeder breaker: a fault past it trips that feeder alone. Set each feeder's relay from the breaker's upper cells with the Power Meter (RELAY SETTINGS). A feeder breaker that fails to open is backed up by breaker failure (50BF): the whole bus opens.\n\n"
						+ "If a GSU stands straight off the bus, 86B also opens the breaker on the GSU's " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " side, so the line cannot feed a bus fault back through it.\n\n"
						+ "A GROUNDING CLAMP SET puts phases A, B and C to ground on a cable, busway or bus duct, or on a big generator's terminals (right-click; again to take them off). On a dead bus it keeps it safe to work on. On a live one it is a bolted fault: a flash, and the relays must clear it. The clamps are rated: a fault cleared in a few cycles leaves them whole, but one that lasts burns them off, and the conductor is UNGROUNDED again.",
				"TRANSFORMER AND GENERATOR DIFFERENTIAL\n\nEvery big transformer of " + Math.round(Tuning.XFMR_87_MIN_VA / 1e6) + " MVA and up (the GSUs and the " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " to " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " power transformer) has its own 87T relay. Its zone runs from the transformer along its cables and bus duct to the breakers on each side. Current that goes into the zone and does not come out at a breaker is going into a fault inside it: 87T opens every one of those breakers at once, and the lockout (86T) holds them open. Once the fault is cleared and the transformer is dead, right-click it with an empty hand to reset; the breakers close again.\n\n"
						+ "The big generators have 87G: grounds or a fault on the generator's own terminals trip it at once. Reset it at its turbine once the fault is cleared.\n\n"
						+ "The Power Meter on a transformer shows 87T ready and how many breakers bound its zone; on a generator, 87G ready.",

				"4.16 KV SWITCHGEAR\n\nA plant's " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " goes out through METAL-CLAD SWITCHGEAR: sections 1 m wide, 3 m tall and 3 m deep, each a draw-out vacuum breaker with its own relay. Stand them side by side facing the same way and their buses join into a lineup. A lineup takes one MAIN section, where the cable from the transformer comes in low on its back, and any number of FEEDER sections, whose cables leave their tops.\n\n"
						+ "Right-click opens or closes a breaker; after a trip it resets and closes. Its relay trips it on overcurrent: 51, sooner the heavier the load (above its PICKUP), and 50 at once at " + Math.round(Tuning.RELAY_50_OF_PICKUP) + " times the pickup. Set the relay from its door (the middle cell) with the Power Meter: see RELAY SETTINGS. On the top cell sneak and right-click steps the breaker's frame. Set the main's pickup above its feeders' so a feeder fault opens only that feeder.\n\n"
						+ "The main also carries the lineup's BUS DIFFERENTIAL (87B): grounds or a fault on the bus open every breaker in the lineup, and they stay locked out until you right-click the main. If a breaker FAILS TO OPEN (beyond its " + Math.round(Tuning.SWITCHGEAR_INTERRUPTING_AMPS / 1000) + " kA interrupting rating, or a stuck mechanism), its breaker-failure relay (50BF) opens the rest of the lineup a few cycles later.\n\n"
						+ "Sneak and right-click with an empty hand RACKS an open breaker: CONNECTED, TEST (it works but carries nothing), DISCONNECTED (drawn out: it cannot close). Racking takes " + Math.round(Tuning.RACK_SECONDS) + " s a position, and the breaker cannot close meanwhile. From a PLC (selector on REMOTE), RACK IN and RACK OUT drive the remote racking motor, so nobody stands at the front of live gear. Rack a feeder out before you work on its cable.",

				"BREAKER RELAY CABINET\n\nThe big " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " and " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " breakers never trip on their own: a relay opens them. In a substation it is the yard's relay panel. Anywhere else, stand a BREAKER RELAY CABINET (1 m wide, 2 m tall) against the breaker. It trips the breaker on overcurrent, 50 and 51, as the switchgear's relay does (see RELAY SETTINGS; its relay is the upper cell).\n\n"
						+ "After a 50 or 51 trip it RECLOSES (79): most line faults are a passing flashover. It closes again after " + Math.round(Tuning.RECLOSE_INTERVALS[0]) + " s, then " + Math.round(Tuning.RECLOSE_INTERVALS[1]) + " s, then " + Math.round(Tuning.RECLOSE_INTERVALS[2]) + " s; a fault still there after the last shot LOCKS it OUT until you right-click it. A " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " cabinet starts with " + Tuning.RECLOSE_SHOTS_DISTRIBUTION + " shots, a " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " one with " + Tuning.RECLOSE_SHOTS_HIGH + "; held closed " + Math.round(Tuning.RECLOSE_RESET_SECONDS) + " s, it counts from the first shot again.\n\n"
						+ "On a " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " breaker it also sheds load (81U): if the island's frequency falls below " + dev.wildcatter.energy.ElectricalStandard.active().loadShedHertz() + " Hz it opens the breaker so the generators survive. Right-click the cabinet to close the breaker again once the cause is gone.",

				"RELAY SETTINGS\n\nA feeder relay (switchgear, breaker relay cabinet, 15 kV feeder breaker) is set from its front panel with the POWER METER. Right-click the relay (a switchgear section's middle cell, a cabinet's upper cell, a feeder breaker's upper cells) to move to the next setting; the one selected shows in [brackets]. Sneak and right-click to step it.\n\n"
						+ "PICKUP: the current the 51 element starts timing at (" + Tuning.RELAY_PICKUP_STEPS[0] + " to " + Tuning.RELAY_PICKUP_STEPS[Tuning.RELAY_PICKUP_STEPS.length - 1] + " A, no higher than the breaker). CURVE: MI, VI or EI (moderately, very, extremely inverse): the steeper the curve, the faster it trips on a heavy fault and the slower on a light overload. DIAL: the time dial, " + Tuning.RELAY_DIAL_STEPS[0] + " to " + Math.round(Tuning.RELAY_DIAL_STEPS[Tuning.RELAY_DIAL_STEPS.length - 1]) + ", scales every time on the curve. 50: the instantaneous trip, a multiple of the pickup, or off. On a cabinet, 79: its reclosing shots, 0 to " + Tuning.RECLOSE_INTERVALS.length + ".\n\n"
						+ "To make devices coordinate, give the one nearer the source a higher pickup or a longer dial, so the one nearest the fault trips first.",

				"LOAD CENTRE AND PANELBOARD\n\nA house's " + Voltage.LOW.label() + " goes through a LOAD CENTRE (200 A main, " + Tuning.LOAD_CENTRE_SPACES + " spaces); a plant's " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " lighting and small loads through a PANELBOARD (225 A main, " + Tuning.PANELBOARD_SPACES + " spaces). Hang it on a wall; the service cable lands on its top or its back. Right-click works the main.\n\nThe panel at the SERVICE is where the neutral meets the earth: drive a GROUND ROD against it (or run ground wire from it to a rod) and its main bonding jumper ties the neutral to ground there, as at a real service entrance. Its readout then says SERVICE. If the service neutral is ever cut, the house's current still comes home through the earth. A panel further on (a sub-panel) gets no rod: its neutral and ground stay apart.\n\n"
						+ "Set PANEL GUTTERS beside it, facing the same way: each holds one branch breaker, and its circuit leaves the gutter's front. Run it out in BRANCH CABLE: it lies along the face you place it against and joins only at its ends, so neighbouring branches stay apart. Gutters chain up, down or sideways, and each space's bus stab alternates phases as a real panel's does. Right-click a gutter with a BRANCH BREAKER to clip it in (load-centre breakers fit only a load centre, panelboard breakers only a panelboard). Right-click to switch it, sneak and right-click to pull an open one out.\n\n"
						+ "A breaker trips on overload or a short. A GFCI BREAKER also trips when the current out on its hot and back on its neutral differ by more than " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.energy.ElectricalStandard.active().groundFaultTripAmps() * 1000) + " mA: current leaking to ground, through a fault or a person. A hand on a bare live wire downstream of it is such a path: the shock still bites, but the GFCI opens the circuit within a couple of cycles.\n\n"
						+ "The main's handle shows through the dead front: up ON, down OFF, centred with a flag TRIPPED. The Power Meter on a breaker also names the device above it and how far they COORDINATE: a branch breaker opens alone only below the main's instant trip ("
						+ Math.round(Tuning.BREAKER_MAGNETIC_MULTIPLE) + " times its rating); a heavier fault opens both. Arc-fault breakers are not made: an arc's signature is not something the grid can carry.",

				"SAFETY SWITCH\n\nThe disconnect beside a " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " motor or machine: a FUSED SAFETY SWITCH, 100 A or 200 A. The line comes in on top and the load leaves the bottom. Right-click works the handle; it breaks full load.\n\n"
						+ "Behind the door are three CLASS J FUSES, one per phase. The door is interlocked: with the handle OFF, right-click with a fuse to fit it, or sneak and right-click to pull them. A fuse rides through a motor start (five times its rating for " + Math.round(Tuning.CLASS_J_SECONDS_AT_2X / 8) + " s) and blows on a short. A blown fuse opens only its phase, and a motor on two phases runs hot: the switch names the phase.\n\n"
						+ "Class J fuses are CURRENT-LIMITING: on a fault over " + Math.round(Tuning.CLASS_J_INSTANT_MULTIPLE) + " times their rating they melt inside the first half cycle and let through only a fraction of the fault's peak, so a breaker upstream of them often never sees it. The switch reads out the last fault: its prospective current, the peak let through and the I²t.",

				"LOAD-INTERRUPTER SWITCH\n\nA " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " LOAD-INTERRUPTER SWITCH (1 m wide, 3 m tall, 2 m deep) opens and closes a cable under load, up to " + Tuning.LIS_LOAD_BREAK_AMPS + " A, but it cannot break a fault. Open it over that and it fails in an arc flash, and is wrecked. The cable comes in on the roof at the back and leaves low on the back.\n\n"
						+ "The FUSED one carries three E-RATED POWER FUSES that clear faults themselves: the usual primary switch of a unit substation. With the switch open, right-click with a fuse to fit it. Like class J fuses they are current-limiting, and the switch reads out what the last fault let through.",

				"TRANSFER SWITCH\n\nAn AUTOMATIC TRANSFER SWITCH keeps a load fed when its normal supply fails. NORMAL comes in on its top, EMERGENCY (a genset) on its back, and the LOAD leaves the bottom. If normal falls below " + Math.round(Tuning.ATS_DROPOUT * 100) + "% it waits " + (int) Tuning.ATS_FACTORY_TDES + " s, then gives a REDSTONE signal: run it to the genset's control panel, which starts on redstone. When the genset is up, the switch opens normal, pauses in the neutral position, and closes onto emergency.\n\n"
						+ "When normal comes back it waits " + Math.round(Tuning.ATS_FACTORY_TDEN / 60) + " minutes (the factory setting), switches back, and lets the engine cool for " + Math.round(Tuning.ATS_FACTORY_TDEC / 60) + " minutes before it drops the signal. Sneak and right-click the bottom with the Power Meter for the SHORT timers (" + (int) Tuning.ATS_TDEN_SECONDS + " s and " + (int) Tuning.ATS_TDEC_SECONDS + " s). Sneak and right-click runs a test transfer.\n\n"
						+ "Sneak and right-click the top with the Power Meter to set how it moves the load between two live supplies (a test, a retransfer). OPEN: break, pause, make; the supplies are never joined. IN-PHASE: open, but only when the two are within " + (int) Tuning.ATS_IN_PHASE_DEGREES + " degrees of each other, so motors are not slammed. CLOSED: make before break, both closed under " + Math.round(Tuning.ATS_OVERLAP_SECONDS * 1000) + " ms, only when the two are within " + (int) Tuning.ATS_CLOSED_DEGREES + " degrees and " + Math.round(Tuning.ATS_CLOSED_VOLTS * 100) + "% voltage; if they never are, it falls back to open after " + (int) Tuning.ATS_SYNC_WAIT_SECONDS + " s. Leaving a dead supply is always open.",

				"SYNCHRONIZING\n\nA set closes its breaker at once onto a dead bus. Onto a live one it must match the bus first: the same voltage, the same frequency and the same phase angle. In AUTO (the default) the panel does it, running a hair fast and closing when it is within " + (int) Tuning.SYNC_MAX_DEGREES + " degrees. In MANUAL (sneak and right-click the stopped panel) you watch the SYNCHROSCOPE on the panel, sneak and right-click to trim the speed, and right-click to close. Close it out of step and the bus slams the alternator into step: the breaker trips with a bang, and a bad enough close wrecks the alternator. Sets on one bus share the load.",

				"PLASTIC WIRE\n\nCraft wire with plastic sheets: it never wears out, at any voltage. Plastic hot and neutral wire are safe to touch, and a plastic " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " or " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " line has no arc reach: you can run it at ground level.\n\nIt carries no more current than bare wire of the same voltage: the rating is the copper.",

				"HIGH VOLTAGE\n\nBREAKERS come for " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " (ratings " + java.util.Arrays.toString(Tuning.BREAKER_AMPS_MEDIUM) + " A) and " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " (" + java.util.Arrays.toString(Tuning.BREAKER_AMPS_HIGH)
						+ " A). They work like the " + Voltage.LOW.label() + " one: in the hot wire, in at the back, out at the front. A 100 kW generator at " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " makes only 24 A, so size the breaker to the line, and put it at the generator.\n\n"
						+ "POLES: a WOOD POLE stands its real height (see POLES AND ARMS) and carries a CROSSARM. Its insulators hold the lines apart. A bare " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " line shocks within " + (int) Tuning.BARE_REACH_MEDIUM + " blocks, " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " within " + (int) Tuning.BARE_REACH_HIGH
						+ ": hang them higher than that above where anyone walks. Poles can be climbed, which puts you next to the line. Or use plastic-insulated line.",

				"SWITCH\n\nA SWITCH opens and closes a hot wire by hand, for servicing: open it before you work on a line. It has no protection and never trips, so a switch alone will not save you from an overload. Put a breaker or fuse ahead of it. (A switch also does not make a line safe by itself: a worker still ground-tests the wire.)",

				"DISTRIBUTION\n\nBetween the " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " transmission line and the houses sits the distribution voltage, " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + ": feeders that run along the roads to the pole transformers. A single-phase tap of the feeder carries line to neutral, " + Math.round(Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.nominal()) + " V, which is the " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " divided by 1.73.\n\nA SUBSTATION steps " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " down to " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " (see SUBSTATION); a small plant's GENERATOR STEP-UP puts its " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " straight onto it. DISTRIBUTION line is rated by its conductor (4/0 ACSR carries " + (int) dev.wildcatter.energy.ConductorSize.ACSR_PENGUIN.amps() + " A) and a bare line shocks within " + (int) Tuning.BARE_REACH_DISTRIBUTION + " blocks. Feeder breakers: " + java.util.Arrays.toString(Tuning.BREAKER_AMPS_DISTRIBUTION) + " A.",

				"OVERHEAD SPANS\n\nOverhead lines are not wire blocks: they are SPANS strung between INSULATORS. Put an insulator on a crossarm or a pole top (a " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " string hangs under an H-frame's crossbeam), right-click it with an empty hand to choose its conductor (A, B, C, N or G), then right-click one insulator and the next with a CONDUCTOR SPOOL. The spool pays out one block of its length per block of span.\n\nA block of span is " + (int) Tuning.SPAN_METERS_PER_BLOCK + " m. Longest spans: " + Tuning.SPAN_MAX_LOW + " blocks at " + Voltage.LOW.label() + ", " + Tuning.SPAN_MAX_DISTRIBUTION + " at " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + ", " + Tuning.SPAN_MAX_HIGH + " at " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + ": put another pole between. Both ends must carry the same conductor. The line sags about 2.5 % of its span.\n\nInsulators are rated: LV 1 kV, DIST 15 kV, HV 138 kV. A line above an insulator's rating FLASHES OVER: it arcs to earth, trips protection, and the insulator shatters. A bare span shocks like bare wire; a COVERED spool makes a plastic-covered span that is safe to touch.\n\nThe flashover's power arc shatters the porcelain once it has carried about " + Math.round(Tuning.INSULATOR_SHATTER_AMP_SECONDS) + " amp-seconds: a few thousand amps for a few cycles, even if the relays clear it at once.\n\nA span carries its conductor's rating (the spool's tooltip). Above it the span heats over minutes; well above it, it anneals, parts and falls.\n\nAn MV spool strings " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " spans, as long as " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " ones, on DIST insulators.",

				"POLES AND ARMS\n\nPoles are true size, one item each: a 30 ft WOOD POLE stands 8 m (service drops), a 40 ft one 10 m (" + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " feeders), a 75 ft one 20 m. Click a CROSSARM onto a pole's side near its top: it bolts on just under the top, across the line, and a pin insulator goes on each end. A third insulator sits on top of the pole, a little higher. Clicked lower, an arm goes where you click (for secondaries).\n\nA " + Voltage.HIGH.label() + " line rides an H-FRAME: two 75 ft poles 4 m apart, a CROSSBEAM clicked onto their tops, an X-BRACE below, and three insulator strings hanging 4 m apart. Click a POLE TRANSFORMER onto a pole and it hangs on it. Break a pole and its arms and insulators come down with it.\n\nGUYS: each span pulls its pole toward the far end; on a straight run the pulls cancel, but a dead end or a corner pulls the top over. The Power Meter on a pole gives its line pull against its class load (30 ft " + "1,900 lbf, 40 ft 2,400, 75 ft 3,700). Past it the pole reads UNGUYED and, left so, leans a step every " + Math.round(Tuning.POLE_LEAN_SECONDS / 60) + " minutes; it does not break. Set a GUY ANCHOR in the ground on the far side from the pull, about as far out as the clamp is high, and string GUY STRAND from near the pole top to it: each guy holds up to about 10,000 lbf, and a guyed pole stands plumb again.",

				"POLE-MOUNT TRANSFORMER\n\nThe last step before a house: a 25 kVA transformer that hangs on a pole (it must stand beside one) and steps the " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " feeder down to " + Voltage.LOW.label() + ". Bring the feeder to its TOP (the high side); the low side is the back, with leg A and the neutral, and the two sides carry leg B (North American worlds: 120/240 V split-phase).\n\nIt is rated: the power on the secondary legs together must stay under 25 kVA. Above that its windings heat as a real transformer's do (IEEE C57.109): at 150 percent it lasts about " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.circuit.TransformerHeating.secondsToFail(1.5, 0) / 60) + " minutes, at 6 times (a motor starting) " + Math.round(dev.wildcatter.circuit.TransformerHeating.secondsToFail(6, 0)) + " seconds, then it burns out. Every rated transformer follows the same rule. Click it to read its loading and how long it has.\n\nA " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " POLE TRANSFORMER is the same 25 kVA unit for an older " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " line, hung and wired the same way.\n\nLEADS: instead of running wire up the pole, string a LEAD from the line's insulator down to the transformer's top with the same conductor spool: right-click the insulator, then the transformer (or a FUSED CUTOUT, whose top contact takes it). A lead reaches " + Tuning.LEAD_MAX_BLOCKS + " m at most, and each part takes one. A unit or cutout hung on a pole comes down with it when the pole is broken.",

				"FUSED CUTOUT\n\nThe pole-top fuse of a " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " feeder: put it in the hot line (in at the back, out at the front) ahead of a pole transformer so a fault takes out the one transformer and not the whole feeder. K-link ratings: " + java.util.Arrays.toString(Tuning.CUTOUT_K_LINKS) + " A (sneak and right-click to choose). When it blows the tube drops open; right-click it with a copper ingot to fit a new link.\n\nA cutout is BARE: its contacts sit at line voltage, and touching a live one is a full shock, grounded or not (linemen use a hot stick). Open the line upstream before you touch it. Breakers, starters and the MCC are enclosed and safe to handle.\n\nSERVICE DROP: from the pole transformer's low side, run wire up to a low voltage insulator, string a conductor spool to an insulator at the house (at most " + Tuning.SPAN_MAX_LOW + " blocks), and bring wire down to the loads. The transformer neutral is tied to earth at the pole.",

				"RECEPTACLES AND PLUGS\n\nPower leaves the grid only through a RECEPTACLE and a PLUG ADAPTER. Wire the receptacle like any load point (leg A or B and the neutral), set the plug adapter of the SAME TYPE against it (it will not stay beside any other), and put another mod's machine or cable beside the plug: on Fabric, any TEAM REBORN ENERGY machine, battery or cable (Tech Reborn and others); on NeoForge, any FE machine, cell or cable (Mekanism and others).\n\nThe plug draws real current: the machines' demand in watts (1 W for each E or FE per tick, set in the config), handed over tick by tick, no more than the circuit gives. It has no protection of its own: if the machines pull too much, the breaker or fuse upstream must trip. Held above its amp rating for " + (int) Tuning.RECEPTACLE_BURN_SECONDS + " seconds the plug and receptacle burn out. On the wrong voltage a plug delivers nothing.\n\nTypes: NEMA 5-15 (120 V 15 A), 5-20 (120 V 20 A), 14-50 (240 V 50 A, both legs), CEE 7 (230 V 16 A), IEC 60309 blue (230 V 32 A). Three-phase: NEMA L21-30 (208Y/120 V 30 A, on the low-voltage tier), L22-30 (480Y/277 V 30 A), IEC 60309 red (400 V, 32 A or 63 A): wire them with three-phase cable.",

				"FREQUENCY\n\nEvery island of generators shares one frequency (" + (int) dev.wildcatter.energy.ElectricalStandard.active().hertz() + " Hz on this world). Load that is larger than the generators can supply pulls it DOWN; spare generation lets it rise. Heavy spinning machines (steam turbines, large engines) change it slowly, light ones quickly. A governor opens the valve as the frequency falls (droop " + Math.round(Tuning.GOVERNOR_DROOP * 100) + "%), and a slow secondary control then brings it back to nominal.\n\nUNDER-FREQUENCY RELAY: put it in the hot wire of a " + Voltage.LOW.label() + " feeder (on a " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " breaker, the BREAKER RELAY CABINET does it). If the frequency falls below " + dev.wildcatter.energy.ElectricalStandard.active().loadShedHertz() + " Hz it opens, shedding that load so the generators survive. A generator whose island stays outside " + dev.wildcatter.energy.ElectricalStandard.active().generatorLowHertz() + " to " + dev.wildcatter.energy.ElectricalStandard.active().generatorHighHertz() + " Hz for " + (int) Tuning.GENERATOR_TRIP_SECONDS + " s trips off: fix the overload and right-click it to restart. Wires, generators and relays show the island frequency.",

				"FUSES\n\nA FUSE is the cheap cousin of the breaker: a strip of metal that melts when too much current flows. It goes in the hot wire like a breaker (in at the back, out at the front), blows faster, and cannot be reset: fix the fault, then right-click it with a copper ingot to fit a new element. Sneak and right-click picks its rating. Use one to protect a branch you do not want to rely on a breaker for.",

				"COOLING TOWER\n\nA steam turbine hands its waste heat to the condensate in its drain. Without cooling, back pressure means it needs " + Math.round(100 / Tuning.UNCOOLED_EFFICIENCY - 100) + "% more steam for the same power.\n\nA tower cell is 4 x 4 m and 6 m high. Put down the COLD-WATER BASIN (your water pipes join it), then click the COOLING FILL, DRIFT ELIMINATORS and FAN DECK on top of it: each stacks into place. The 3 m fan has a " + Math.round(Tuning.COOLING_FAN_WATTS / 100) / 10.0 + " kW " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " three-phase motor; run a cable up to the front of the fan deck. It only cools while the fan has power; you can watch it turn. Click the turbine to see if it is cooled.",

				"CONDUCTORS\n\nA wire carries ONE conductor, shown by its coloured band: A red (the hot of a single-phase circuit), B orange, C blue, N black (neutral), G green (ground). Right-click a wire with an empty hand to change which conductor it carries. A circuit needs its conductors running out to the load and back.\n\nSPLIT-PHASE (North American worlds): a transformer's low side is centre-tapped. A and B are the two legs, 180 degrees apart. Each leg is " + Voltage.LOW.label() + " to the neutral N, and A to B is double that. A load on leg A and a load on leg B share the neutral, and it carries only the DIFFERENCE between them: equal loads leave it empty. IEC worlds have a single phase and no leg B.\n\nThe ground conductor G is the earth itself: a bare wire carrying another conductor that touches it is a ground fault.",

				"CONDUCTOR SIZES\n\nWire comes in sizes, each its own item. The bigger the conductor, the more current it carries and the less voltage it loses over a long run:\n12 AWG 20 A, 10 AWG 30 A, 6 AWG 65 A, 2 AWG 115 A, 4/0 230 A, 500 kcmil 380 A (copper building wire, 120 V to 480 V). An 800 A BUSWAY carries a genset's output.\n\nAbove 480 V lines are ACSR (aluminium on a steel core): #2 180 A, 1/0 240 A, 4/0 340 A, 336 kcmil 530 A, 795 kcmil 900 A. Heavy conductors sag more, so their spans are shorter. Craft a bigger size from smaller wire of the same kind; the breaker must never be rated above the wire it guards.",
				"THREE-PHASE\n\nGenerators make three phases, A, B and C, a third of a turn (120 degrees) apart, plus the neutral N. Each phase is " + Voltage.LOW.label() + " to the neutral; between two phases it is 1.73 times that (" + Math.round(Voltage.LOW.lineToLine()) + " V).\n\nSpread single-phase loads over A, B and C: when the three are equal, their currents cancel in the neutral and it carries nothing. A lamp or a one-pole breaker takes whichever ONE phase reaches it.\n\nThe big transformers are three-phase. Voltages above " + Voltage.LOW.label() + " are named line to line (4.16 kV, 12.47 kV, 138 kV); a wire shows its line-to-neutral volts too.\n\nA big three-phase generator (a " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " cube) shares its rating among its three phases: each stator phase carries only a THIRD of it. (A lone " + Voltage.LOW.label() + " engine or turbine is a small single-phase set: any one phase may take all of it.) Pile the load on one phase and that winding overheats (" + Math.round(Tuning.STATOR_I2T_SECONDS / 0.69) + " s at 130 percent, about 12 s at twice its share) and the machine TRIPS. Right-click it to restart once the load is spread out.",
				"480 V AND CABLE\n\nIndustry runs on " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " three-phase (" + Math.round(Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.nominal()) + " V to neutral). A PAD-MOUNT transformer steps the " + Voltage.DISTRIBUTION.label() + " feeder down to it (300 kVA), or to 208Y/120 V for shops (75 kVA). A UNIT SUBSTATION takes it from " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " in a plant (1,000 kVA). Both are true size: a pad-mount fills 2 x 2 x 2 m, its high side on the left as you face its doors and its low side on the right, each at the bottom front cell's outer side or underneath; the unit substation is a 4 m lineup, " + Voltage.MEDIUM.label() + " at one end and " + Voltage.INDUSTRIAL.label() + " at the other.\n\nTHREE-PHASE CABLE carries A, B, C, N and G in one insulated block: lay it like wire. A single wire touching a cable takes the one conductor it carries, so a cable can split into three phase wires (that is how a 138 kV line leaves a substation transformer for three insulators: HIGH-VOLTAGE CABLE off its bushings, then a riser per phase). A THREE-POLE BREAKER sits in the run and opens all three phases at once when any one of them faults.\n\nThe THREE-PHASE HEATER (15 kW) needs all of A, B and C.",
				"TAILINGS CELL\n\nLay a floor and walls of CELL LINER and stand a DECANT TOWER on the floor. Pipe tails slurry to the tower on steel pipe; it fills the cell and sends water back on a water pipe. It holds " + (int) (Tuning.CELL_KG_PER_BLOCK / 100) / 10.0 + " t a block. A missing liner block: it seeps and stops until you mend it.\n\nA bigger pond settles more: the tower takes " + Math.round(Tuning.CELL_SLURRY_KG_PER_TICK * 72) + " t/h of slurry on up to " + Math.round(Tuning.CELL_FLOOR_PER_RATE) + " m2 of floor, and as much again for each " + Math.round(Tuning.CELL_FLOOR_PER_RATE) + " m2 more.\n\nSLURRY PIPE (600 mm): a big plant's slurry line, rated about " + Math.round(Tuning.SLURRY_PIPE_M3_S) + " m3/s; it carries no gas and does not join steel pipe. AIR HEADER (600 mm): blower air along a row of flotation cells; it does not join instrument air tubing.",
				"PROCESS WATER PUMP\n\nThe water pump on a 480 V three-phase motor, for a plant with no 110 V supply. Put it against water and run water pipe to what needs it.",
				"MOTORS\n\nPumps, fans, pumpjacks, rigs and process units run on induction motors. A motor draws nothing while its machine has no work. Starting, it pulls " + Math.round(Tuning.MOTOR_LOCKED_ROTOR_MULTIPLE) + " times its running current for " + Math.round(Tuning.MOTOR_START_SECONDS) + " seconds at full voltage (the inrush); on a sagging supply its torque falls with the square of the voltage and the start runs longer (at 80 percent, about 3 seconds). Then it settles at a power factor of " + Tuning.MOTOR_POWER_FACTOR + ".\n\nA three-phase motor turns the way its phases come round. Swapped phases run it BACKWARD: sneak and right-click it with an empty hand to swap two leads at its terminal box. Lose one phase and a running motor STALLS, drawing its starting current until something trips. Big motors start gentler on a SOFT STARTER or a DRIVE (next pages).",
				"MOTOR CONTROL\n\nA MOTOR STARTER sits between the 480 V line (its back) and one motor (its front). Right-click or a redstone signal starts and stops it. Inside: a motor circuit protector that opens at once on a short (" + Math.round(Tuning.MCP_MULTIPLE) + " times the setting), a contactor, and an OVERLOAD RELAY. Set its dial (sneak and right-click) to the motor's full-load amps; it trips on a sustained overload, within " + Math.round(Tuning.OVERLOAD_CLASS_SECONDS) + " s at six times the setting, never at or below 115 %.\n\nA MOTOR CONTROL CENTER is an INCOMING SECTION (main breaker, fed on its back or top) with up to " + Tuning.MCC_MAX_BUCKETS + " BUCKETS. The sections are real size, 2.3 m tall: the INCOMING SECTION (main breaker, fed on its top or the back of its bottom) and STARTER SECTIONS to its right, touching, all facing the same way. Click an MCC BUCKET into an empty space of a starter section: three to a section, one per metre of height. Each bucket is a starter for one motor: its cable leaves the back of its own space. A gap in the line ends the bus; breaking a section drops its buckets. Soft-starter and drive buckets click in the same way (see SOFT STARTERS AND DRIVES).",
				"SOFT STARTERS AND DRIVES\n\nA SOFT STARTER (480 V cabinet, MCC bucket, or 4.16 kV cabinet) holds a motor's starting current at its LIMIT dial, " + Tuning.SOFT_START_LIMITS[0] + " to " + Tuning.SOFT_START_LIMITS[Tuning.SOFT_START_LIMITS.length - 1] + " times the full-load amps (sneak and right-click with the Power Meter). Less current means less torque, so the start takes longer. When the motor is up to speed the bypass closes: BYPASSED. Line in on the top or the back of its top cell, motor out the back of its bottom cell.\n\nA VARIABLE-FREQUENCY DRIVE (480 V cabinet, MCC bucket up to 100 hp, or the 4.16 kV lineup) ramps the motor up over " + Math.round(Tuning.DRIVE_RAMP_SECONDS) + " s at no more than its running current, and the line sees a power factor of " + Tuning.DRIVE_LINE_POWER_FACTOR + ". It takes constant power, so on a sagging bus it draws more current; below " + Math.round(Tuning.LAND_RIG_UNDERVOLTAGE * 100) + " % voltage it stops until the voltage is back. Held over " + Tuning.DRIVE_CURRENT_LIMIT + " times the full-load amps for " + Math.round(Tuning.DRIVE_LIMIT_SECONDS) + " s it trips.\n\nThe 4.16 kV drive is three sections side by side, facing the same way: the INPUT TRANSFORMER (line in at its outer end or its top), the POWER CELLS, then OUTPUT AND CONTROL (motor out at its outer end). Set the cabinet's or the control section's dial (sneak and right-click) to its motor's full-load amps.",
				"DC: RECTIFIERS AND BUS BARS\n\nA RECTIFIER holds its DC current at its SETPOINT (sneak and right-click steps it, " + Math.round(Tuning.RECTIFIER_SETPOINTS_KA[0]) + " to " + Math.round(Tuning.RECTIFIER_SETPOINTS_KA[Tuning.RECTIFIER_SETPOINTS_KA.length - 1]) + " kA), at whatever voltage the cells need, up to " + Math.round(Tuning.RECTIFIER_MAX_DC_VOLTS) + " V. Set a cell against it and it takes that cell's current by itself.\n\n"
						+ "Further away, run DC BUS BARS (4 kA or 16 kA copper) from its terminals, + over - on its east side, to the cell's: + to +, - to -. Bars that touch join, whatever their axis; a bar bridging the + and - runs is a short, and the rectifier trips (right-click resets it). A bar carrying more than its rating heats and burns open.\n\n"
						+ "The DC is not grounded: with no fault each pole sits at half the voltage from earth. A bar touching a ground wire is a GROUND FAULT, and the rectifier names the pole. Then the other pole is at full voltage to earth, and from " + Math.round(Tuning.DC_SHOCK_MIN_VOLTS) + " V DC a bare bar shocks.",
				"ON THE WALL\n\nSmall gear is drawn at its real size. Click a BREAKER, SWITCH, FUSE, RELAY or MOTOR STARTER against the side of a block and it hangs on that wall, its line running along the wall: in from the left, out to the right as you face it. Placed on the floor it stands on a stand, its line running the way you face.\n\nRECEPTACLES, PLUGS, LAMPS and HEATERS go on whatever face you click: a wall, the floor or the ceiling. They still take their wires on any side.",
				"PLCs\n\nA PLC cabinet runs a real program. It needs 24 V: a CONTROL POWER SUPPLY on ordinary mains wire, reached by CONTROL CABLE. Click a CPU module into the cabinet, then input and output modules: they fill slots 0, 1, 2 and on.\n\nSlot n owns 16 bytes from n x 16, so channel 3 of an input module in slot 1 is %IX16.3.",
				"WIRING A PLC\n\nA control cable makes one run. Where a run must split, use a JUNCTION BOX: a cable touching more than two things is a BAD JOINT, and the cabinet names it.\n\nClick the cabinet with an empty hand. TERMINALS lists what its cables reach: pick a signal and land it on a channel. Sneak with an empty hand to pull the last module.",
				"CABLE AND 24 V\n\nA control cable is 50-pair: 98 cores for signals. An on-off signal takes one core, a 4-20 mA loop or a counter two. A cable that is full refuses the next signal: lay a second cable to the same box, or put a remote drop out there.\n\nThe supply gives 10 A. Lamps, horns and solenoids draw from it; past 10 A it shuts off for a second and tries again. The door window shows the modules seated and the RUN lamp.",
				"PROGRAMS\n\nCODE is IEC 61131-3 structured text. CHECK compiles it here. DOWNLOAD sends it, and leaves the CPU in STOP. RUN and STOP are the key.\n\nPROGRAM MAIN\nVAR go AT %IX0.0 : BOOL;\ncoil AT %QX16.0 : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\ncoil := go;\nEND_PROGRAM",
				"HAND, OFF, AUTO\n\nClick a starter with the SELECTOR KEY to step its selector. HAND is its own button and redstone, as ever. OFF stops it. AUTO gives it to the PLC, whose RUN signal then commands it.\n\nA device in AUTO stops if it hears nothing for half a second: a cut cable, no 24 V, STOP and a CPU fault all look alike. A PLC can never hold off an overload, and a trip still needs its hand reset.",
				"WHEN IT STOPS\n\nDIAGNOSTICS names the fault, its program and its line. A program that takes too long trips the WATCHDOG: the CPU stops and its outputs drop. STOP, then RUN clears it.\n\nONLINE watches and writes variables, and FORCES inputs and outputs. Release what you force: the program cannot see past it.",
				"LADDER AND FBD\n\nA project holds program units in any language, and they call each other: +ST, +LD, +FBD. In a ladder, pick a rung and use the toolbar: NO and NC contacts, BOX, BRANCH around what is selected, COIL, / for a negated coil, S and R. VARS holds its variables. Green is power, from the CPU's own values. A rung can carry a LABEL; >> jumps forward to it while it has power, and RET ends the unit. With nothing selected, the kind button makes a unit a FUNCTION.",
				"ONLINE CHANGE\n\nDOWNLOAD stops the CPU. ONLINE CHG swaps the project with it running, each variable of the same name keeping its value, so a plant runs on through an edit.\n\nIn an FBD, click an output pin and then an input pin to wire them. Drag a block to move it, and the empty sheet to pan. The number on a block is its place in the execution order.",
				"CHARTS\n\n+SFC is a sequential function chart. STEP and TRANS chain down the sheet; select a transition and add STEP again for a parallel branch, or a step and add TRANS for a choice. Click a foot pin and then a head pin to wire anything else: a line back up shows as a jump.\n\nA condition can read a step's time: S1.T >= T#5s.",
				"ACTIONS\n\nSelect a step and press ACTION. Qualifiers: N while active, S and R to set and reset, L for a limited time, D after a delay, P for one scan, and P1, P0, SD, DS, SL.\n\nAn action is a BOOL it drives, or press BODY to give it structured text: it runs while active and once more as it ends, reading its own NAME.Q.",
				"MOTORS AND VALVES\n\nMOTOR_CTRL takes a START demand, RUNNING, TRIPPED and AUTO, and gives RUN. No feedback in 15 s is FAIL_START; feedback lost is FAIL_RUN. They latch FAULT until RESET. Outside AUTO it asks for nothing and raises nothing.\n\nVALVE_CTRL does the same between two limit switches. Neither can hold off a trip.",
				"CARDS AND FILES\n\nClick a MEMORY CARD on a cabinet to seat it. Sneak with an empty hand pulls it first. PROJECT has TO CARD, and FROM CARD, which downloads and leaves the CPU in STOP. A card holds the program, not the wiring.\n\nEXPORT writes PLCopen XML or structured text to wildcatter/plc in the game folder. IMPORT reads it into the editor; DOWNLOAD sends it.",
				"ANALOG SIGNALS\n\nAn AI8 reads 4-20 mA as a word from slot x 16: 4 mA is 0, 20 mA is 32000. An open or failed loop reads 32767, so check for it. An AO4 writes the same scale. The words are WORDs: WORD_TO_INT.\n\nA TRANSMITTER clamps to the machine behind it. Click to step what it reads. Set its 4 and 20 mA values in TERMINALS, with its tag.",
				"DRIVE SPEED\n\nIn AUTO, a drive follows a SPEED REF landed on an AO4, down to 20 %. Flow follows speed, and a pump lifts nothing below 30 % against its head. Power falls with the cube of speed, so a pump at a third of its speed draws a thirtieth of its power.\n\nPID holds a level: PV from the transmitter, OUT to the reference.",
				"VALVES\n\nA CONTROL or ON-OFF valve moves on air: AIR COMPRESSOR, AIR DRYER, then AIR TUBING to its top. Lose air and its spring takes it to its fail position; sneak-click sets open or shut. A MOTOR-OPERATED valve wants 480 V, and stays put without it. A run of pipe stops at a shut valve. In HAND, click to move one.\n\nA WATER DAY TANK empties through a valve touching it.",
				"POWER FROM A PLC\n\nBreakers and switchgear give CLOSE and OPEN coils, on LOCAL or REMOTE with the selector key. A set takes RUN and a CLOSE PERMIT, and reads kW on 125 % of its rating; its trims shift its share of the load. A PLC never overrides a trip: a tripped breaker takes no close until a hand resets it.",
				"HMI PANELS\n\nAn HMI PANEL reads any PLC on its NETWORK CABLE, which needs a COMM module in the cabinet. EDIT lays out values, bars, lamps, buttons, motors, valves and trends from tags, such as MAIN.PV. ALARMS adds a limit on a tag. ACK acknowledges one, and SHELVE puts it aside for ten minutes. The history keeps a hundred events.",
				"REMOTE I/O\n\nA REMOTE I/O DROP is a rack with no CPU, on the network cable, with its own 24 V and control cables. Click it empty-handed to set its rack number. Rack 1's slot 0 is slot 12, so its first input is %IX192.0; each rack takes 12 slots more. Cut the network and its outputs stop arriving, so what they run falls back. A large CPU reaches further racks. A rack answers one PLC: the first to reach it, until that one has been silent a second.",
				"PLC TO PLC\n\nName a PLC under NET, then take another's tags: MAIN.FLOW = PLC-2/MAIN.FLOW. The copy runs every half second, and a lost link keeps its last value and shows FAILED, so check for that where it matters. An HMI asks by station too: PLC-2/MAIN.FLOW. A marker such as PLC-2/%MW10 reads and writes as a register.",
				"COMING\n\nSwitches and panels.\n\nThis book will grow as they do."
		);
	}

	private static String hearts(float damage) {
		float hearts = damage / 2;
		return hearts == Math.floor(hearts) ? String.valueOf((int) hearts) : String.valueOf(hearts);
	}
}
